{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop","id":1216156,"title":"Sorcery Workshop","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-07T08:49:56-07:00","id":1216156,"title":"Sorcery Workshop","content":"If this exists in another thread, I apologize for spamming. But since I haven't found one, I'm creating it here.<br /> <br /> I want to know how you, fellow Exalted player, go about creating new spells. From the mundane to the monumental, what is your process when developing a new spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:01:31-07:00","id":1216160,"title":"","content":"This is one of the things the book lacks guidance for.<br /> <br /> It is currently not even possible, rules as written.<br /> <br /> The Devs have said they will approach the subject on the Sorcery focused book.<br /> <br /> That being said, the previous editions have a wealth of ideas, and many people convert from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:11:53-07:00","id":1216162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1216160#post1216160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is currently not even possible, rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily think that's true. Given the examples in the core book, we should use those as starting points, rather than an exhaustive list of spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:28:04-07:00","id":1216172,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4164_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4164\" data-vbnamecard=\"4164\">Lukkychukky</a> here. Though not explicit, it gives plenty of different types of spells at each circle and from that you can derive a working, though not perfect, design space for how spells can be built. Combined with stuff from the Q&amp;A thread (I can post examples from the nishkyra database when I get home). And it gives you something that generally tells you the level of scope from each circle, the kinds of scale it\u2019s effects can encompass, and the cost of each. Is it definitive? No, and each table will need to come to consensus on it on their own. But to say just because it\u2019s not explicitly stated \u201cThese are the rules\u201d does not mean it\u2019s not impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:24:37-07:00","id":1216193,"title":"","content":"I understand what both of you are saying.<br /> <br /> Its just that RAW, there is no way to create new spells. There are two RAW ways of learning new spells, from mentors or from &quot;scrolls&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can homebrew your way of inventing new spells, but it is not RAW.<br /> <br /> And RAW is what I was talking about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:27:34-07:00","id":1216195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1216193#post1216193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand what both of you are saying.<br /> <br /> Its just that RAW, there is no way to create new spells. There are two RAW ways of learning new spells, from mentors or from &quot;scrolls&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can homebrew your way of inventing new spells, but it is not RAW.<br /> <br /> And RAW is what I was talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally get you, my point is that Exalted with its specific carve outs such as the golden rule make RAW less sticky for me then say Pathfinder. Just my 2 cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:37:17-07:00","id":1216204,"title":"","content":"For sure, thats why I suggested an easy way to go about it is to convert other editions' spells.<br /> <br /> Now for rules on how to invent them, there are none.<br /> <br /> One idea is to make it like a Sorcerous Working, maybe Ambition 3 of the same circle as the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T10:42:52-07:00","id":1216207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1216204#post1216204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sure, thats why I suggested an easy way to go about it is to convert other editions' spells.<br /> <br /> Now for rules on how to invent them, there are none.<br /> <br /> One idea is to make it like a Sorcerous Working, maybe Ambition 3 of the same circle as the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>But my point is you can establish new spells in setting w/o working, though if you want the character to create X spell a working is a good avenue. Just because it\u2019s not published I don\u2019t feel is a significant barrier to development, but ymmv as I love doing Homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T11:51:23-07:00","id":1216247,"title":"","content":"The one spell I created was based on Wood Dragon\u2019s Claw, but instead of creating an artifact claw hand, it created an artifact pellet crossbow from wind and sand and contract.<br /> <br /> More conceptually, Sorcery should be, above all else, weird. One way to do that is to take a Thing, like butterflies, fire, clouds, skin, a kraken, and so on, and give it some of the properties of a completely different Thing, like obsidian, a bird, a carriage, bronze, magma, and so on. This \u201cThing which can act like some totally different Thing\u201d concept seems to be fertile ground for all kinds of spells and makes a good jumping off point for brainstorming your own spell and Working ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T11:53:15-07:00","id":1216249,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty sure that, in the Ask the Devs thread, Vance said \u201cJust let them pay xp and learn the new researched spell.\u201d So, presumably the training time for a spell is long enough to devise your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T12:48:08-07:00","id":1216268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page138\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page138\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page138\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page138 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1101248#post1101248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> Creating a spell doesn't require any rolls or XP expenditures other than those you spend to learn the spell - it's something your character does in the narrative that doesn't really benefit from being modeled mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a> has the right of it, though I wouldn't presume the training time is enough to create a new spell. He just said it is a narrative thing that probably won't get modeled mechanically.<br /> <br /> But in reality, I don't know, haven't given it much thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T13:47:29-07:00","id":1216289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1216193#post1216193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand what both of you are saying.<br /> <br /> Its just that RAW, there is no way to create new spells. There are two RAW ways of learning new spells, from mentors or from &quot;scrolls&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can homebrew your way of inventing new spells, but it is not RAW.<br /> <br /> And RAW is what I was talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like saying there's no RAW way to climb ladders. It's technically true that there's no specific widget for it in the ruleset, but it still falls under the umbrella of an existing rule (in this case, the Orichalcum Rule).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-07-2018, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:00:55-07:00","id":1216294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1216289#post1216289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's like saying there's no RAW way to climb ladders. It's technically true that there's no specific widget for it in the ruleset, but it still falls under the umbrella of an existing rule (in this case, the Orichalcum Rule).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be if the book didn't specify the way to acquire new spells, but it does. So it is a bit more nuanced than that. Though I agree it is not a big problem, and it should be easy to figure out with the ST/Table.<br /> <br /> Pg. 178<br /> <br /> &quot;and learning spells requires a mentor or a text copy of the spell in question and many hours of intense study.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T06:51:12-07:00","id":1216618,"title":"","content":"Sorcery has to be strategic. <br /> <br /> The closest thing to a fireball spell is flight of the Brilliant raptor. Only its not a fireball spell. Its basically an artillery spell in a bronze age setting, where most ranges are in at least a few hundred meters. The Flight of the Brilliant Raptor's range is basically 1,800 yards. I.e. 1.6 kilometers. Basically, the most basic fireballs spell in the arsenal hilariously outranges any possible weaponry in the bronze age weaponry. You need gods or charms to shoot that far. <br /> <br /> Sorcery isn't just something you do. For almost sorcery spell, there's almost someting that makes it stand out. Something that prevents it from being generic and makes each spell unique and fluffy. The fireball spell doesn't just fling fireballs. It makes you into artillery capable of firing out a bird on fire that explodes and kills your target and everyone around him. That spell you use to change your appearance? Its not just appearance. Mannerisms, tics, anima, all are changed as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T07:00:28-07:00","id":1216620,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>, those are all good points! Exalted puts much more emphasis on spells being unique and extremely powerful. Most other TTRPG spells, if ported into Exalted, would be covered by most likely the least of any of the Charm trees. So, how would you go about designing a new spell with those things in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:33:24-07:00","id":1216669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lukkychukky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1216620#post1216620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>, those are all good points! Exalted puts much more emphasis on spells being unique and extremely powerful. Most other TTRPG spells, if ported into Exalted, would be covered by most likely the least of any of the Charm trees. So, how would you go about designing a new spell with those things in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Scale. Terrestiral circle sorcery is supposed to affectabout 1 to 5 people <br /> <br /> 2. Fluff. There's a spell for translation. But its not just a translation spell. It also creates a mask that you wear, that makes your voice reverberate in a supernatural way. This way, the mask not only looks kickass, but also adds an extra effect. And another thing, like the translation spell for texts. Not just one that makes the word makes sense. But its conjures a mouth and eye to scan the text, and then the mouth speaks the text in your native language. Basically, the same effect. But the implementation is far different. <br /> <br /> 3. Strategic level. Let's have several examples. And keep in mind, this is the bronze age. The one where having good steel weapons are counted as something incredible. Or at least, expensive.<br /> <br /> A. Horse that travels over Earth and Water. <br /> <br /> A tireless horse that travels over both the lakes, seas, and solid ground. This is a big thing, despite appearances. Normal horses tire. They are expensive to both maintain, take care of, and feed. Half the time with a horse, you're walking, cause a horse that is forced to gallop all day dies. A horse can break a leg or lose a shoe. This one doesn't. <br /> <br /> A horse like this in real life in the medieval ages would be worth its weight in gold. It basically means you can probably travel thrice the distance, with lesser cost. Its not just a single benefit. Its several, all clustered together. Sorcery spells can benefit you in several ways at once. <br /> <br /> B. Ramparts of obedient Earth. <br /> <br /> Something that can let you create 3 story high walls of earth, with no need for bricks, kilns, workmen, or mortar. Just some saplings. remember, this is Creation. There's only muscle power. Stuff like this would take weeks to build, entire quarries, and at least dozens of men. But you do it in, like, an hour. Sorcery spells can do grand workings, in ways charms cannot. <br /> <br /> C. Infallible Messenger. <br /> <br /> This spell, in all effects, basically makes it so that you have instant sms messaging and email across the entirety of creation. Think about it. In a medieval age setting like Creation, getting information and messages out is slow, hard work. It takes weeks, its unreliable, the message might get lost, or get intercepted. This spell, in effect, lets you bypass all that. The same thing is done with the wooden face. It lets you basically carry out teleconferences. I don't think I need to stress the level of use this has in a place like Creation. <br /> <br /> 4. Sorcery is, in effect, miracles. Not miracles of inhuman skill, but instead miracles. Like the way moses parted the seas or created manna. External, miracles, like the way that you see in the bible. You want to be able to have super sword skills? Nope. Not going to happen. You want to conjure flaming swords that fly up and impale your enemies? You're right on. <br /> <br /> 5. I think sorcery should have some... subsets. Think of Conan the Barbarian. Those kind of sorcerers. Those kind of sorcerers that would die in any melee focused battle. But they excel in preparation. Look at the buffs. Look at the stuff like Sorcerer's irresistble puppetry and disguise of the new face. The sorcerer is the dude that walks up to the melee focused exalted, gets cut in half... only to reveal it was some poor sap that got controlled by Puppetry and got face changed by Disguise of the New Face. Look at the buffs. Mists of Eventide. Impenetratable Frost Barrier. Burning eyes of the offender. All are buffs that take time to cast and use. A sorcerer should not be able to truly excel in a stand up fight. But he should, when given the chance to prepare, become a nightmarishly dangerous enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T02:05:31-07:00","id":1217299,"title":"","content":"So anyway... <br /> <br /> How about an anti tech spell, made by a lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T02:58:38-07:00","id":1217311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217299#post1217299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about an anti tech spell, made by a lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>What would that even mean? Everything we have made, everything we have, is technology; sails are tech, the wheel is tech, <i>clubs</i> are tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-10-2018, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T03:05:51-07:00","id":1217313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217311#post1217311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would that even mean? Would spears stop working in its vicinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies.<br /> <br /> Simply put, celestial spell made by a lunar really fitting in the barbarian mindset. He makes this spell, to damage the tools of the realms armies.<br /> <br /> It's basically a heart of darkness. A field that, once deployed, will start eroding away at any form of technology.<br /> <br /> A wooden staff? Falls apart in a day or so, rotting away.<br /> <br /> A sword of steel, forged in the realms most advanced forges? Rusts away to dust in several minutes.<br /> <br /> Artefacts, magical materials, and weapons held by exalted do not fail.<br /> <br /> How about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 05-10-2018, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:29:18-07:00","id":1217342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217313#post1217313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, celestial sword made by a lunar really fitting in the barbarian mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which &quot;barbarian mindset?&quot; Every tribal culture in the setting uses tools; even the Dune People fashion breathing tubes to facilitate their day-sleep.<br /> <br /> In what way does rejecting tool use fit said mindset?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217313#post1217313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He makes this spell, to damage the tools of the realms armies.<br /> <br /> It's basically a heart of darkness. A field\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it a field, or is it a sword?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217313#post1217313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026that, once deployed, will start eroding away at any form of technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I've used tools to divert a river for irrigation purposes, what happens when the Lunar's sword/field hits the river?<br /> <br /> Will cows exposed to this heart of darkness start crumbling?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217313#post1217313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wooden staff? Falls apart in a day or so, rotting away. <br /> <br /> A sword of jadesteel, forged in the realms most advanced forges? Rusts away to dust in several minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does the sturdier thing made of a magical material crumble away faster than the flimsier thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217313#post1217313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artefacts, magical materials, and weapons held by exalted do not fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why did the magical material fail?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-10-2018, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:41:30-07:00","id":1217346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217342#post1217342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which &quot;barbarian mindset?&quot; Every tribal culture in the setting uses tools; even the Dune People fashion breathing tubes to facilitate their day-sleep.<br /> <br /> In what way does rejecting tool use fit said mindset?<br /> <br /> Is it a field, or is it a sword?<br /> <br /> So if I've used tools to divert a river for irrigation purposes, what happens when the Lunar's sword/field hits the river?<br /> <br /> Will cows exposed to this heart of darkness start crumbling?<br /> <br /> Why does the sturdier thing made of a magical material crumble away faster than the flimsier thing?<br /> <br /> Then why did the magical material fail?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies. Corections have been made. <br /> <br /> What i mean was.... the realm legions have higher levels of equipment. And barabarian tribes, having much less infrastructure and exalts, don't. So this spell is used as a way of leveling the playing field.<br /> <br /> Also, the spell doesn't damage natural weapons. So beastmen tribes can use claws, superior strength, and fangs to kill the soldiers. Meanwhile, the Realm legions have realized that their steel swords and pikes have fallen apart in their hands, and are trying to CQC giant monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:50:41-07:00","id":1217351,"title":"","content":"I think that the rationale Accelerator was going for is that more tecnhologically advanced things deteriorate faster.<br /> <br /> Thats why a sword crumbles away faster that a staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T06:10:34-07:00","id":1217356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217351#post1217351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the rationale Accelerator was going for is that more tecnhologically advanced things deteriorate faster.<br /> <br /> Thats why a sword crumbles away faster that a staff.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, that's what i meant. <br /> <br /> Its not just what it is. Its also how it was made. <br /> <br /> Two swords. One made by a master smith from a podunk village. Another made in the heart of the Realm, using thaumaturgically treated tools. <br /> <br /> The one made by the Realm dies faster. <br /> <br /> Its a way to upend the entire scale of battle, and basically rewrite the rules of the game. Now the side with lower tech wins. Or at least, gets less disadvantaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T10:18:31-07:00","id":1217436,"title":"","content":"I really don\u2019t think that Exalted has the necessary degree of technological disparity to make an anti-tech field make much sense. A field that causes metal to rust or degrade very quickly would be much simpler to define and describe and accomplish most of the same goals without ending up in complex philosophical arguments about the nature and definition of technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T15:56:52-07:00","id":1217515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1217436#post1217436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don\u2019t think that Exalted has the necessary degree of technological disparity to make an anti-tech field make much sense. A field that causes metal to rust or degrade very quickly would be much simpler to define and describe and accomplish most of the same goals without ending up in complex philosophical arguments about the nature and definition of technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, damn it. Maybe this would work better in a exalted modern setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T10:39:22-07:00","id":1218010,"title":"","content":"Ok, I wrote down some stuff: <br /> <br /> The Blight of Autochthon - Celestial Circle spell<br /> <br /> There are 2 versions of this spell, both invented by the same Lunar. The Lunar, unhappy with the difference in equipment quality and infrastructure levels between the Realm, the civilized countries, and the barbarian hordes that he lead against the Realm. This spell is meant to level the field.<br /> <br /> It comes in two forms.<br /> <br /> All is Dust: <br /> <br /> Cost: 20m Duration: 1 day<br /> <br /> All things break down. Metal rusts. Wood rots. Clothes become moth eaten. Flowers wilt. Stones are ground down to powder by time. And so do all things made by human hands. Focusing the energies of rot and making the sign of Blight, which signifies the sickness of Autochthon, the sorcerer creates a field, of one mile in radius centered around him or several hundred yards away from him. Within the field, all things made via artificial processes are slowly eroded by the energies within this field. Every minute, every single man made object or structure gains unsoakable, unblockable damage as they decay. The spell has no effect on natural things, such as rock formations or a sharp branch picked up by a hunter.<br /> <br /> The levels of damage absorbed by each object is dependent on the object's complexity and advancement. An axe, carved from a flint stone and a branch with a hole bored into it and secured by twine, would receive one level of damage. On the other hand, a suit of plated mail or a stainless steel sword forged in the artisan-crucibles of the Realm would receive 5 per minute<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the size of the spell can be altered, along with the rate of destruction. Doubling the area of effect would halve the rate the damage occurs, and vice versa. <br /> <br /> Return to medieval style<br /> Cost: 60m Duration: 12 hours<br /> <br /> The sorcerer makes the sign of the blessing of Autochthon, made to represent his love of tools and technology and carved upon the tools of the jadeborn. And then he inverts it.<br /> <br /> In a scream of horror sounding unsettingly like the ones released by blightborn, the functioning of technology within an area of 2 miles wide ceases to function. Firedust refuses to ignite. Knives do not cut. Gears do not turn. Everything made by man, every tool, every crutch weakening them, is rendered useless. Alternatively, the caster could decide the level of technological sophistication allowed within the area. For example, he could allow the usage of knives but not guns. Or he could allow the usage of combustion engines. But not electronics. <br /> <br /> At the end of duration, there is no damage done to the items and structures affected. <br /> <br /> The only thing usable are claws and natural weapons. And those, the Lunar and his subordinates know how to use quite well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T10:53:00-07:00","id":1218613,"title":"","content":"Objects don't have health levels in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T19:34:20-07:00","id":1218774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1218613#post1218613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objects don't have health levels in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what? Nevermind all this. I made a spell idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T02:22:16-07:00","id":1218839,"title":"","content":"For the game I am in my ST told me he is open to me developing a spell I want to make myself. Me and him are still working out the details but essentially require some minimums.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Spell - Occult 3 / Essence 2 + / +1 ability related to field spell is in / 2 weeks per circle minimum.<br /> Celestial Spell - Occult 5 / Essence 3 + / +1 ability related to field spell is in / 2 weeks per circle minimum.<br /> Solar Spell - Occult 5 / Occult/Lore Specialty that is appropriate / Essence 5 + / +1 ability related to field spell is in / 2 weeks per circle minimum.<br /> <br /> Another aspect we have been tooling around with is spell creation using crafting project style rules but using Occult or Lore instead. Still up in the air right now. He is fortunately pretty open to me making a spell as long as it fits the power level and fits sorcery theme of unique effects and abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T05:58:38-07:00","id":1218878,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12440_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12440\" data-vbnamecard=\"12440\">drakor</a>, I really like that write-up! Very neat to see some of the minimum prereq\u2019s Laid out so cleanly like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Co-Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.twitter.com/deliberativepod\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>!<br /> Follow us on <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/thedeliberativepodcast\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook</a>!<br /> Follow us on the <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com\" target=\"_blank\">Web</a>!<br /> Like what we do? Support us on <a href=\"http://patreon.com/thedeliberative\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4164-lukkychukky","name":"Lukkychukky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T07:13:53-07:00","id":1218899,"title":"","content":"An idea for a spell for modern times: <br /> <br /> What about a spell for travelling through cyberspace and such? <br /> <br /> And a hound of the five winds that can travel through the internet and kill people through phones and laptops","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T22:33:50-07:00","id":1220439,"title":"","content":"Ok, um, I got some things I wrote down when I was thinking of 'resources'. <br /> <br /> GAINING THE RICHES BELOW - SOLAR CIRCLE SPELL<br /> Motes: 60m <br /> Duration: Permanent: <br /> <br /> The sorcerer goes to the geomantic center of the area he wishes to cast this spell in, and carves out the sigil of the Kukla on a rock from that area. And then he repeats the process at each of the area's 4 cardinal directions, chanting the hymns of rebirth, of disaster bringing forth riches. After that, he goes to the center, and performs the sign of destructive change while standing in front of the center sigil. It is at this point in time that the sorcerer decides what kind of underground resources he wishes for. Then the sorcerer flees for his life, for at this moment, the very earth around him quakes. <br /> <br /> Earthquakes and tremors rock the area defined by the four sigils at the edges, with small after shocks affecting the nearby area, enough to knock down straw and mud houses, and enough to crack brick ones. Within the area, any building that is not made of the magical materials is shake apart, while manses lose power and shut down as the dragon lines are reordered. All tunnels and previous excavations into the earth are collapsed and reordered, and everything in the general area at the ground level is completely destroyed and remade. <br /> <br /> After a month of the catalysm, the shaking stops. And the miracle appears. What the miracle manifests as, depends on what the sorcerer wanted. If the sorcerer desired a diamond mine, he would be able to literally pick up diamonds just by digging into the ground, less than a foot from the surface. If he wishes for gold, he can walk towards the river, and find hundreds of thousands of nuggest of pure gold, released by the eruptions and overtuning of the earth. Any minerla, metal, or any resource which can be taken from the ground itself, can be created with this spell. With the exception of the five magical materials. Those can only be brought closer and more accessible to the surface, not created wholesale by this spell. <br /> <br /> A/N: A question. Should this be celestial or Solar? I think being able to own the richest mines in creation should be a good thing, but in bronze age societies, food is always more important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T23:15:43-07:00","id":1220448,"title":"","content":"Why put a mote cost on it? It looks a lot more like a Ritual spell, to me; or, do you intend for it to be cast in combat time?<br /> <br /> Also, what happens when someone distorts it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T03:08:18-07:00","id":1220483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1220448#post1220448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why put a mote cost on it? It looks a lot more like a Ritual spell, to me; or, do you intend for it to be cast in combat time?<br /> <br /> Also, what happens when someone distorts it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, why not? <br /> <br /> I'm not sure. I got several ideas. 1. Everything is lava. 2. the earthquakes go out of control, destroying the entire area and everything around it. 3. The earth essence collapses, basically creating a giant sinkhole in the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T03:31:47-07:00","id":1220489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1220483#post1220483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2022 The area it covers is never specified beyond a quadrilateral whose points are defined by where the sigils are placed.<br /> \u2022 How long it takes to carve the sigil of the Kukla is not specified, either.<br /> \u2022 You have to move from one point on the map, to another, to <i>another</i>, to <i><b>another</b></i>, to <u><i><b>another</b></i></u>, and then back to the first point, to cast this spell. Even if no one contests your movement and you can mark your Kukla-rocks instantaneously, the fight has a really good chance of being over before you get to cast it.<br /> \u2022 It's a good idea to describe the environmental hazard characters caught in the tremors will face. (Which, as a reminder, the sorcerer will have to endure while fleeing the area of the spell.)<br /> \u2022 Aside from subjecting a larger area to a month of constant earthquake, what's the point of performing this spell in a larger area, if casting it in a one-meter square gets me the same diamond mine?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1220483#post1220483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. the earthquakes go out of control, destroying the entire area and everything around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that it's an earthquake that is powerful enough to damage brick buildings and lasts for an entire month, that's not much of a distortion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T05:07:28-07:00","id":1220509,"title":"","content":"Oh man. Hmm... you have a point. narratively, this is supposed to basically have the same role as benediction of archgenesis, i.e. terraforming. <br /> <br /> I suppose that for the area, its the same. 50 square miles. <br /> <br /> Maybe reduce the earthquakes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T16:44:55-07:00","id":1220656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1220439#post1220439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, um, I got some things I wrote down when I was thinking of 'resources'.<br /> <br /> GAINING THE RICHES BELOW - SOLAR CIRCLE SPELL<br /> Motes: 60m<br /> Duration: Permanent:<br /> <br /> The sorcerer goes to the geomantic center of the area he wishes to cast this spell in, and carves out the sigil of the Kukla on a rock from that area. And then he repeats the process at each of the area's 4 cardinal directions, chanting the hymns of rebirth, of disaster bringing forth riches. After that, he goes to the center, and performs the sign of destructive change while standing in front of the center sigil. It is at this point in time that the sorcerer decides what kind of underground resources he wishes for. Then the sorcerer flees for his life, for at this moment, the very earth around him quakes.<br /> <br /> Earthquakes and tremors rock the area defined by the four sigils at the edges, with small after shocks affecting the nearby area, enough to knock down straw and mud houses, and enough to crack brick ones. Within the area, any building that is not made of the magical materials is shake apart, while manses lose power and shut down as the dragon lines are reordered. All tunnels and previous excavations into the earth are collapsed and reordered, and everything in the general area at the ground level is completely destroyed and remade.<br /> <br /> After a month of the catalysm, the shaking stops. And the miracle appears. What the miracle manifests as, depends on what the sorcerer wanted. If the sorcerer desired a diamond mine, he would be able to literally pick up diamonds just by digging into the ground, less than a foot from the surface. If he wishes for gold, he can walk towards the river, and find hundreds of thousands of nuggest of pure gold, released by the eruptions and overtuning of the earth. Any minerla, metal, or any resource which can be taken from the ground itself, can be created with this spell. With the exception of the five magical materials. Those can only be brought closer and more accessible to the surface, not created wholesale by this spell.<br /> <br /> A/N: A question. Should this be celestial or Solar? I think being able to own the richest mines in creation should be a good thing, but in bronze age societies, food is always more important.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> I love the idea of the spell effect on this. It got some creative thought on my end going. I wanted to share some thoughts I had on it with you as well! Really nice idea ! I hope some of the idea I gave below can be helpful as well.<br /> <br /> Gaining the Riches Below - Solar Circle Sorcery<br /> Cost: 60m 3wp Ritual - Requires: Geomancy 5<br /> Duration Permanent<br /> <br /> The sorcerer designates a central point for this spell and places or selects a large stone (10ft x 10ft min.) as the spell anchor. Once selected or placed the sorcerer begins to carve the names of the materials desired into the rock in old realm well as carving essence channels across the rocks surface over the course of at least a full day. The sorcerer must also carve the expected dimensions the spell will cover up to a 10 mile radius on the highest portion of the stone and embed small pieces of the desired metals and minerals he desires to find within the carved map area on the stone. With preparations complete the sorcerer travels to the edge of the area he has designated to be effected and begins to perform shaping actions as he walks the entire perimeter of the area he has chosen. The shaped essence is sent rushing towards the stone and causes the mineral names carved into the essence channels to begin to glow softly as each one activates under the influx of gathering essence as the geomancy in the area begins to alter in order to manifest the sorcerer's desires.<br /> <br /> Mechanical Effect: The sorcerer can designate up to (Permanent Willpower) metals/minerals that will begin to proliferate in the area he has demarcated. Large deposits of the desired metals/minerals will begin to form due to the geomantic changes wrought by the spell. As long as the anchor stone is not destroyed the area will renew an equivalent amount of material equal to (Resources 5) of each metal/mineral every year. If the anchor stone is destroyed the area marked will deplete as normal. due to the geomantic changes that this spell brings this effect can not be redone within 1,000 miles of an active spell and all plant life will grow at half its normal rate in the area while the spell is active.<br /> <br /> Control Spell: the sorcerer can complete this spell within a 100 miles of another active one. Of note however if they do, the area designated past the first will have the plant life in the marked area wither and die for as long as the spell is in effect due to the geomancy being further disrupted.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T19:20:47-07:00","id":1220683,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I forgot. You can make it regenerative....<br /> <br /> Isn't stuff like a ten mile area kinda huge? Won't the sorcerer die of exhaustion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T17:29:40-07:00","id":1233857,"title":"","content":"2 ideas for spells: <br /> <br /> 1. Weakened version of benediction of arch genesis. Let's you transform desert into grassland, as a shaping effect. In a ripple, the land itself changes and grass is brought into being. Pros: fast. Cons: smaller area and no changing the climate. <br /> <br /> 2. Conjure up animals. Any animals. A shittier version of demon of the first circle. No need for a roll-off. Animals can be permanent or temporary. Either conjure up a horde of rabbits to devastate the countryside, or cows to cook into a steak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T10:22:39-07:00","id":1234040,"title":"","content":"As to anti-technology spells? Creation has multiple layers of fallen golden ages, in which even mortal artifice was much more advanced. Maybe it's not particularly useful in the Age of Sorrows (unless you're being stormed by Haslanti glider troops, then it's pretty great!) but when it was invented, it might've been highly effective.<br /> <br /> Just say that it makes stone knives useless within ten minutes. and Haslanti air boats within one minute. If it matters, twice that time will completely unmake it, Things completely unmade by this effect are reduced to raw materials - steel swords to lumps of iron ore, buff coats to uncured hides, houses to logs, branches and rocks. <br /> <br /> It's a slow-burn, wide-area Shattering Grasp with a hate-on for anything more advanced than sticks and stones, and a little knock-on effect (because even straightforward sorcery should be a bit weird)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T10:30:19-07:00","id":1234042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1233857#post1233857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 ideas for spells:<br /> <br /> 1. Weakened version of benediction of arch genesis. Let's you transform desert into grassland, as a shaping effect. In a ripple, the land itself changes and grass is brought into being. Pros: fast. Cons: smaller area and no changing the climate.<br /> <br /> 2. Conjure up animals. Any animals. A shittier version of demon of the first circle. No need for a roll-off. Animals can be permanent or temporary. Either conjure up a horde of rabbits to devastate the countryside, or cows to cook into a steak.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2--I...think this is a spell. I forget its name. It's terrestrial cirlce, IIRC, and summons a number of animals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T11:42:17-07:00","id":1234058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1234042#post1234042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 2--I...think this is a spell. I forget its name. It's terrestrial cirlce, IIRC, and summons a number of animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Army of the Wild. <br /> <br /> But Army of the wild doesn't let you summon up an army of desert-adapted yeddim to let you carry an entire caravan across the sea. Neither does it allow you to summon up acid-spitting scorpions that can burrow and work as landmines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T14:30:34-07:00","id":1234090,"title":"","content":"<b>FIREY EMPOWERMENT OF WEAPONS</b><br /> Cost: 10 motes<br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> <br /> The sorcereress makes the sign of weapons, while speaking the first word the Elemental Dragon of Fire spoke. At this, searing essence billows out, and the weapons of her companions, up to her Essence X 2, glow red hot with fire. The fire increases the damage caused by the weapons, adding her occult score in dice of damage.<br /> <br /> The heat, though damages the weapons. Each time the spell ends, the sorceress rolls her occult vs Difficulty (6 - Essence). On a failure, the weapons empowered by the spell are destroyed and are melted into slag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T15:47:39-07:00","id":1234426,"title":"","content":"Hm! If that damages artifacts (it is quite possible for fire to burn hot enough to damage artifacts, as Sekhem's current wielder well knows) that's pretty bad news for Exalts, but I could easily see a mortal (Ifrit-initiated, probably) sorceress busting it out for her retinue. If it doesn't damage artifacts, we have a new favorite for the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T16:34:13-07:00","id":1234439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1234426#post1234426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm! If that damages artifacts (it is quite possible for fire to burn hot enough to damage artifacts, as Sekhem's current wielder well knows) that's pretty bad news for Exalts, but I could easily see a mortal (Ifrit-initiated, probably) sorceress busting it out for her retinue. If it doesn't damage artifacts, we have a new favorite for the Wyld Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Maybe I should add in various sub effects, like being able to add damage to creature of darkness or set things they hit aflame. <br /> <br /> And create a mass combat version of the spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T17:23:17-07:00","id":1234456,"title":"","content":"Question. How would one write a spell that grants mutations and merits, both to willing and unwilling subject? I'm fairly sure that there were potions that granted immortality, and spells that granted resilience in mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T18:13:36-07:00","id":1234474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1234456#post1234456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. How would one write a spell that grants mutations and merits, both to willing and unwilling subject? I'm fairly sure that there were potions that granted immortality, and spells that granted resilience in mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Potions would be a working :P<br /> <br /> A spell--I'd make a unique spelll for types of mutations. A spell that gives people the aspect of a beast is different then one that turns them into a warp spasm--although thinking on it, how many buff other spells are there in exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T18:15:21-07:00","id":1234476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1234474#post1234474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Potions would be a working :P<br /> <br /> A spell--I'd make a unique spelll for types of mutations. A spell that gives people the aspect of a beast is different then one that turns them into a warp spasm--although thinking on it, how many buff other spells are there in exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do self buffs count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T19:24:57-07:00","id":1234493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1234476#post1234476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do self buffs count?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, that's what the other in buff <i>other</i> was for. I might be wrong, but its intreasting to me that there's no spells that enhance someone besides the sorcerer as a primary function ( a few spells help others with control effects).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T20:02:20-07:00","id":1234502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1234493#post1234493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, that's what the other in buff <i>other</i> was for. I might be wrong, but its intreasting to me that there's no spells that enhance someone besides the sorcerer as a primary function ( a few spells help others with control effects).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I suppose it's because sorcery is meant for yourself. I mean, its in the corebook. The spells are meant to benefit the player.<br /> <br /> There is no reason why sorcery can't buff others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T09:34:39-07:00","id":1245129,"title":"","content":"Idea. How about a sorcery that blesses buildings?<br /> <br /> When the spell is cast on the workshop, it counts as 1 assistant and the workshop level rises. When cast on a hospital, patients get bonus dice to resisting disease and recovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T02:01:02-07:00","id":1246217,"title":"","content":"CREATING THE STONE LABRYINTH<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp<br /> <br /> The sorcerer raises a hand, and shouts the Word of the Lost. At this, a labryinth is conjured around the sorcerer. The maze can be made of anything. In the jungle, hedges grow into shape. In the ocean, water rises up into walls. On land, earth reshapes itself into a maze. In the air, the space itself warps. The difficulty of navigating the maze, is (Sorcerer's essence + Intelligence + Occult), and anyone trapped inside must roll (intelligence + survival) to get through the maze. If the person wins, he is able to navigate the maze without getting lost, and is able to either find the sorcerer, find other people, or exit the maze. <br /> <br /> At an interval defined the sorcerer, whether via ticks, actions, hours, or days, a new part of the maze is added. The maze starts off enclosing a 100 yard by 100 yard square, and each interval increases by the size by a hundred yards. This continues on, until each side of the maze is 1000 yards in size. As each interval passes, the maze is reshaped, forcing whoever is trapped inside to reroll. If they fail, they are once again, lost. <br /> <br /> This maze is useless against anyone who can fly. Or jump good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T02:11:00-07:00","id":1246219,"title":"","content":"RESURRECTING THE FALLEN CITY - CELESTIAL<br /> Cost: Ritual<br /> Duration: 1 day<br /> <br /> The sorcerer takes flag stones of a ruined city, and beats the tune of reborn civilisations and of new beginnings. The stones and material of the city dances with the tune, repairing themselves. Broken and shattered rubble brings itself back together into walls and streets. Cracked pavement mends itself. Ashes reform into books. Sand melts and remolds into glass. At the end of the ritual, the entire city is restored, or up to 40 x 40 miles in area, whichever is smaller. The spell cannot repair shattered geomancy, destroyed artifacts, or broken artifice. The only things it can repair, are up to thaumaturgical products. Thus, only cities can be made, but the first age is lost forever. <br /> <br /> CONJURING SUSTENANCE FROM NOTHINGNESS<br /> Cost: 15m<br /> Duration: 1 day<br /> <br /> The sorcerer first designates a group of people who he wants to feed, which can be of any magnitude. However, the base costs of the spell starts at 15 motes, and for every increase in magnitude, 3 motes are added.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer then makes the mudra of the god of feasting and speaks the word in Ancient Realm for 'food'. In his hand is conjured a blue silk bag, thrown onto the ground in front of him. The bag opens... and out floats plates, bowls, cups, forks, spoons, chopsticks, knives, platters, trenchers, and jugs, all containing the best mortal food there is. The cutlery and food all contain food that a particular member of the group loves the most, and floats to him/ her. The food is always filling, well-received, and is never rots away.<br /> <br /> Anyone who receives food from the bag, and eats it, does not suffer hunger penalties for the next (sorcerer's essence + occult) days, and receives 2 dice to resisting hardship<br /> <br /> TREE OF BOUNTY - terrestrial circle sorcery<br /> Cost: 10sm<br /> <br /> The sorcerer picks a fruit, any fruit. Then throws it up into the air, while murmuring the words which the Emerald Mother spoke when the first trees emerged from Creation. The fruit scatters into ashes, which land on the ground. From there, a tree grows. It does not matter the condition. A tree meant for the east, could survive in the firey mountains of the South or in water-logged soil of the West. It will grow. It then grows to a stately tree, several dozen meters in height, with hundreds of branches, all bearing fruit. When the fruit is plucked, another is created within minutes, growing to maturity before the bearer's eyes. <br /> <br /> The fruits are always healthy, sweet, and large, and the tree itself is immune to disease and parasites. After (sorcerer's occult score) years, the tree's regenerative ability fades. It is still immune to disease, and the fruits are still the best possible, but it no longer regrows its fruits in seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T14:14:38-07:00","id":1246741,"title":"","content":"For Creating the Stone Labyrinth, compare Malediction of the Distorted Compass -- Celestial, I think, for a similar effect. I like the image of a sorcerously growing and shifting maze, but it seems more like a working than a spell. Also, you haven't said how high the walls are.<br /> For Conjuring Sustenance From Nothingness, compare Food From the Aerial Table -- again, a similar effect, though I don't remember what Circle this is. Not a huge nitpick, I just think the conceptual territory is already covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T00:11:06-08:00","id":1267209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1246741#post1246741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Creating the Stone Labyrinth, compare Malediction of the Distorted Compass -- Celestial, I think, for a similar effect. I like the image of a sorcerously growing and shifting maze, but it seems more like a working than a spell. Also, you haven't said how high the walls are.<br /> For Conjuring Sustenance From Nothingness, compare Food From the Aerial Table -- again, a similar effect, though I don't remember what Circle this is. Not a huge nitpick, I just think the conceptual territory is already covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good god. I just realized something. These were meant to be celestial sorcery spells!<br /> <br /> I just saw this, and thought I had to emulate it.<br /> <br /> Butterflies to Chrysalides Bombardment<br /> Cost: 35m<br /> <br /> Target: Area (250 yard radius, centred on target point within 1 mile of sorcerer)<br /> <br /> <br /> A Silurian innovation, this spell uses the motonic principles of Death of Obsidian Butterflies, but expands them up to the Sapphire Circle. As the sorcerer shapes the spell, a collection of butterflies, some in obsidian, others cast in a faintly fluorescent greenish-yellow glass begin to spiral the caster, their flight spelling out the Word of Complexity, which represents sudden change in faraway places from small alterations.<br /> <br /> <br /> When the character releases the spell, they roll their Perception + Occult, adding their Essence in automatic successes. On the completion of the spell, the butterflies arc up into the air, coming down a tick later on the target location as a great swirling cyclone of enormous glass butterflies, each butterfly anywhere from a foot to a yard across. Everything within 250 yards of that target is subject to the attack. The attack descends from above, so any cover must be at least an inch of stone overhead to protect; the butterflies are quite capable of cutting through the roofs \u2013 and upper floors \u2013 of most Second Age structures to shatter on the inhabitants within.<br /> <br /> <br /> Characters defend against Butterflies to Chrysalides Bombardment as if it was a hand-to-hand attack, and each attack is independent, so magic which protects only one person will not protect others subjected to the same attack. Treat the butterflies as rolling a number of attack successes equal to what the sorcerer\u2019s player rolled, -1 for each two dice of penalties that circumstances impose. In cases of thick fog or a heavy low cloud level, characters may have to reflexively roll (Perception + Awareness), Difficulty 1, to avoid it being a surprise attack. The attack inflicts 12L, plus any extra successes on the attack roll as per usual.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, this spell does not merely litter the ground with broken glass (though it does so, much like Death of Obsidian Butterflies). The butterflies, in their brief flight, release small lumps of igneous rock, around the size of a man\u2019s fingernail, which litter the ground within the affected area. Compared to the brightness of the glass, they are dull and mundane. However, moving or Dashing across the affected area, for the next lunar month, risks life and limb. Each tick where the character moves or Dashes requires a (Perception + Awareness) roll, at a difficulty of half the sorcerer\u2019s Essence, and the roll may only be made if the character is aware of the danger. Failure means that a character\u2019s shadow has fallen on one of the chrysalides. From it, grows a spear-like bush made of fused butterflies made of black and green glass, directly pointed at the obstruction to the light, which then blossoms in a newly formed canopy at head height. This is modelled as a hand-to-hand attack against everything within 3 yards, which counts as having rolled the same number of successes as the original attack, and which inflicts +6L damage. The spear-bush created are living creatures, but will wither and die, turning brittle, if not fed on blood. The Imperial Legions have strict policies for what is to be done if it is found that a legion has wandered in such a formation, often including the use of Earth Aspects to turn over the soil, safely defusing the unhatched chrysalides. Sapphire Circle Countermagic safely defuses all the chrysalides in the area; Emerald Circle Countermagic can disarm all the ones in an area equal to that produced by a casting of Death of Obsidian Butterflies, allowing a formation to be moved through a so-covered area. Once the lunar month has passed, the unhatched chrysalides turn inert, but any spear-bushes that have grown remain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T22:02:58-08:00","id":1267506,"title":"","content":"Hey guys. An idea. Voodoo doll. Grab a link, stuff it into a doll, and then you can extract information from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T01:10:09-08:00","id":1267786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1246217#post1246217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CREATING THE STONE LABRYINTH<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp<br /> <br /> The sorcerer raises a hand, and shouts the Word of the Lost. At this, a labryinth is conjured around the sorcerer. The maze can be made of anything. In the jungle, hedges grow into shape. In the ocean, water rises up into walls. On land, earth reshapes itself into a maze. In the air, the space itself warps. The difficulty of navigating the maze, is (Sorcerer's essence + Intelligence + Occult), and anyone trapped inside must roll (intelligence + survival) to get through the maze. If the person wins, he is able to navigate the maze without getting lost, and is able to either find the sorcerer, find other people, or exit the maze.<br /> <br /> At an interval defined the sorcerer, whether via ticks, actions, hours, or days, a new part of the maze is added. The maze starts off enclosing a 100 yard by 100 yard square, and each interval increases by the size by a hundred yards. This continues on, until each side of the maze is 1000 yards in size. As each interval passes, the maze is reshaped, forcing whoever is trapped inside to reroll. If they fail, they are once again, lost.<br /> <br /> This maze is useless against anyone who can fly. Or jump good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the concept, but not a fan of the execution. It is rediculously powerful, especially for sorcerers who can safely keep casting spells from the center of the maze. Unless the target have insane int+survival, it is highly unlikely they will ever be able to navigate the maze. The caster can CHOOSE the interval and the interval can be ticks? So even if they manage to make the roll, they instantly get lost again. Why is the maze a square? And why is it measured in yards? Since it is not a ritual it seems to be made to be used in combat scencarios, so range bands would be more appropriate. How is it useless against those who can fly and jump? It warps space itself!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1246217#post1246217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RESURRECTING THE FALLEN CITY - CELESTIAL</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a balance issue with this one, just seem like something already covered by either workings or crafting charms. I would make change the time to a week and make it a day for those who have it as control spell or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1246217#post1246217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CONJURING SUSTENANCE FROM NOTHINGNESS</div> </div> </div> </div>So it is not as however many they like, but for up to BG 5? Magnitude is not same as size. And what is with the duration? It is not a ritual. And it should have some WP cost. If it never rots and it is super food they keep people fed for days.... yeah, no. I would have it go bad after a day and have the keeping people fed long part be for control spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1246217#post1246217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TREE OF BOUNTY</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good working. But as written as a spell, a sorcerer can create infinite food in seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T06:02:23-08:00","id":1267816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1267786#post1267786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a good working. But as written as a spell, a sorcerer can create infinite food in seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... like food of the aerial table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T09:41:28-08:00","id":1267882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1267816#post1267816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... like food of the aerial table?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, for simplicitys sake, lets assume the sorcerer always gather 10 motes per action and that each action is 3 seconds.<br /> The tree sounds massive. Sounds like one could easily feed 100 people from a harvest.<br /> Lets assume fruits grow back in 10 minutes. (you stated both it takes minutes and seconds, lets assume minutes)<br /> <br /> Food of aerial table: Feed 10 people per 3 seconds invested by the sorcerer. Food tastes bland.<br /> Tree of bounty: A single tree take 3 seconds from the sorcerer. Every 10 minutes it feed about 100 people (fruits from a branch could probably feed at least one person, you said hundreds of branches but lets go with 100). So every day, assuming it being harvested continually (an elemental bound to harvest sounds fitting) it can feed 100x6x24=14400 people per day at least. for 3-5 years. The fruits are always healthy and with several trees, you can get plenty of variation and you can also make dishes.<br /> <br /> They are on completely different levels. I assume it not having a WP cost is an oversight, otherwise, the sorcerer could make 20 of these in a minute. This spell is much stronger than the solar circle spell &quot;Benediction of Archgenesis&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T09:58:33-08:00","id":1267890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1267506#post1267506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys. An idea. Voodoo doll. Grab a link, stuff it into a doll, and then you can extract information from them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like a great concept. Rather think cursing fit better than torture. Here is a rough idea for a terrerstrial, possibly celestial spell:<br /> <br /> Effigy of the unfortunate fool<br /> Cost: Ritual, 2wp<br /> <br /> The sorcerer craft a doll of the target while continually cursing their name and existance, pouring their vitriol into their creation. (if the craftsmanship of the doll matters, roll craft. But for the purpose of the spell, it does not matter.). This ritual takes about an hour and requires the sorcerer to know the name, appearance (a description is not enougth but a well made painting is) as well as something that links to the target (hair, bodily fluids, something important to the person...) witch is integrated into the doll.<br /> <br /> Once per day until the seasons turn, the sorcerer may insert a needle into the doll. At that very moment, some minor misfortune befall the victim. In most circumstances, this means stubbing their toe, stepping in a deep puddle, falling out of bed or some such harmless but annoying incident. However, if timed right, it can have distastrous consequences. The king speaking to his subject suddenly get shit on by a bird, the warrior about to deliver the killing blow step on uneven ground and slips and so on. The exact consequences is up to the storyteller, but as a rule of thumb, If the target is in the middle of performing an action, that action take a -(occult) penalty. In combat, dropping their weapon or falling prone or some such is more fitting.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer may only have (essence) dolls. If more are made, one lose their magic (sorcerer picks).<br /> <br /> Sorcerers who know this as their controll spell do not need a link to their target and can have (essencex3) dolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T17:17:58-08:00","id":1268106,"title":"","content":"Woah woah woah. No link? Too overpowered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T19:14:42-08:00","id":1268126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268106#post1268106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah woah woah. No link? Too overpowered</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd at least require it work like Silent Words, where you can do it without a link <i>as long as you've met them</i>, and require a linkless version to have to keep encountering them for repeated use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:23:10-08:00","id":1268169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1267890#post1267890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds like a great concept. Rather think cursing fit better than torture. Here is a rough idea for a terrerstrial, possibly celestial spell:<br /> <br /> Effigy of the unfortunate fool<br /> Cost: Ritual, 2wp<br /> <br /> The sorcerer craft a doll of the target while continually cursing their name and existance, pouring their vitriol into their creation. (if the craftsmanship of the doll matters, roll craft. But for the purpose of the spell, it does not matter.). This ritual takes about an hour and requires the sorcerer to know the name, appearance (a description is not enougth but a well made painting is) as well as something that links to the target (hair, bodily fluids, something important to the person...) witch is integrated into the doll.<br /> <br /> Once per day until the seasons turn, the sorcerer may insert a needle into the doll. At that very moment, some minor misfortune befall the victim. In most circumstances, this means stubbing their toe, stepping in a deep puddle, falling out of bed or some such harmless but annoying incident. However, if timed right, it can have distastrous consequences. The king speaking to his subject suddenly get shit on by a bird, the warrior about to deliver the killing blow step on uneven ground and slips and so on. The exact consequences is up to the storyteller, but as a rule of thumb, If the target is in the middle of performing an action, that action take a -(occult) penalty. In combat, dropping their weapon or falling prone or some such is more fitting.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer may only have (essence) dolls. If more are made, one lose their magic (sorcerer picks).<br /> <br /> Sorcerers who know this as their controll spell do not need a link to their target and can have (essencex3) dolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a clever idea. But you misunderstand what I meant by torture. <br /> <br /> I meant 'information extraction'. <br /> <br /> One of the most important things is information. And a sorcerer can get those easily. Repairs spells for destroyed papers. Translation spells. Scrying spells. Calling up ghosts and binding them. Summoning elementals and demons and using them as immaterial spies. Talking to animals. <br /> <br /> Basically, you make a doll of a person, using a link... and then the person will tell you everything the person knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T03:13:00-08:00","id":1268214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268126#post1268126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd at least require it work like Silent Words, where you can do it without a link <i>as long as you've met them</i>, and require a linkless version to have to keep encountering them for repeated use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it would be more approprite that &quot;if the sorcerer have a major/defining negative intimacy towards the target or something the target stands for (for example hatred for the wyld hunt and the target is a shikari of the wyld hunt) they do not require a link&quot;. In other words, if the hatred they pour into the doll is genuine. Bear in mind, in order to use the spell effectively, you need to spy on them, easy to do with demons/elementals against normal people, but those with power are likely to find out. Then there is the whole messing with causality thing and the sidereal who may take offence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T03:17:44-08:00","id":1268215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268169#post1268169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a clever idea. But you misunderstand what I meant by torture.<br /> <br /> I meant 'information extraction'.<br /> <br /> One of the most important things is information. And a sorcerer can get those easily. Repairs spells for destroyed papers. Translation spells. Scrying spells. Calling up ghosts and binding them. Summoning elementals and demons and using them as immaterial spies. Talking to animals.<br /> <br /> Basically, you make a doll of a person, using a link... and then the person will tell you everything the person knows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No problem if done right. What to be careful about is not wrecking investigation and a major part of socialize (read intentions). All charms relating to lie spotting, forcing people to tell the truth and finding out intimacies could be made pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T03:57:41-08:00","id":1268220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268215#post1268215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No problem if done right. What to be careful about is not wrecking investigation and a major part of socialize (read intentions). All charms relating to lie spotting, forcing people to tell the truth and finding out intimacies could be made pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>..... I guess so. But let's be honest here. There's always going to be overlap. Incantation of restoration can overlap craft charms. Stormwind rider overlaps athletics for long distance travel. Bronze overlaps with resistance, etc. <br /> <br /> You just need to make sure that it's unwieldy and a bit hard to use. <br /> <br /> Maybe you get blood. Or skin flakes. Or hair. Nice. <br /> <br /> It only applies to stuff when the person last interacted with or had it. Take hair from a person? If he changes plans tomorrow, you won't know. <br /> <br /> Obviously, you can do more. Maybe you can a only ask a certain.... <br /> <br /> Hey. <br /> <br /> The sorcerer can ask the shadow questions about the target; one question by default, plus an extra question per ten additional motes spent to tithe the shadow in payment. It has limited knowledge: the shadow knows and can describe the surfaces it has fallen upon, it knows the lies the target has spoken in its presence, and it knows what the target hates (her negative Intimacies). The shadow gives clear answers to short and direct questions, but cryptic answers to vague or open-ended questions. Usually, one question will give the sorcerer knowledge of one location, one major lie, one negative Intimacy, or something of equivalent worth.<br /> <br /> Maybe like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T04:11:50-08:00","id":1268223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1267786#post1267786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like the concept, but not a fan of the execution. It is rediculously powerful, especially for sorcerers who can safely keep casting spells from the center of the maze. Unless the target have insane int+survival, it is highly unlikely they will ever be able to navigate the maze. The caster can CHOOSE the interval and the interval can be ticks? So even if they manage to make the roll, they instantly get lost again. Why is the maze a square? And why is it measured in yards? Since it is not a ritual it seems to be made to be used in combat scencarios, so range bands would be more appropriate. How is it useless against those who can fly and jump? It warps space itself!</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw man. <br /> <br /> Maybe... its weaker against essence users? I just wanted to make it so that one can actually visualize the maze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T10:30:42-08:00","id":1268326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268220#post1268220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ..... I guess so. But let's be honest here. There's always going to be overlap. Incantation of restoration can overlap craft charms. Stormwind rider overlaps athletics for long distance travel. Bronze overlaps with resistance, etc.<br /> <br /> You just need to make sure that it's unwieldy and a bit hard to use.<br /> <br /> Maybe you get blood. Or skin flakes. Or hair. Nice.<br /> <br /> It only applies to stuff when the person last interacted with or had it. Take hair from a person? If he changes plans tomorrow, you won't know.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you can do more. Maybe you can a only ask a certain....<br /> <br /> Hey.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer can ask the shadow questions about the target; one question by default, plus an extra question per ten additional motes spent to tithe the shadow in payment. It has limited knowledge: the shadow knows and can describe the surfaces it has fallen upon, it knows the lies the target has spoken in its presence, and it knows what the target hates (her negative Intimacies). The shadow gives clear answers to short and direct questions, but cryptic answers to vague or open-ended questions. Usually, one question will give the sorcerer knowledge of one location, one major lie, one negative Intimacy, or something of equivalent worth.<br /> <br /> Maybe like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, how about this?<br /> <br /> The Tell-Tale Shade<br /> Cost: Ritual, 3wp<br /> Duration: Until Sunrise<br /> <br /> Using a link to their target, the sorcerer creates a shade of essence and darkness. This shade is not a spirit, but a simple mimicry of who the link belong to. It can only be ordered by the sorcerer to stay, follow or tell a tale. It wont attack or otherwise help the sorcerer and a single point of damage witch effect spirits destroy it. When it is created, the sorcerer roll (Occult+intelligence) where the successes are the number of tales it can tell before fading.<br /> <br /> The tales the shade tell are of the memories of the target. The sorcerer can specify a specific event (the day you were wed) or a time and date. Typically, only the more memorable moments are told but if the memory is recent (less than a year) the sorcerer can specify to know mundane things (what did you eat for breakfast 23 days ago?)<br /> <br /> At sunrise, the shade fades away along with the link and any remaining tales. During calibration, the shade lasts until calibration is over. <br /> <br /> People who are already dead can be the target of this spell but they tend to forget about the day of their death. Someone who has been a target of this spell can't be made a target again until next month except during calibration.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer who know Tell-Tale Shade as her control spell may choose to experience the memories rather than being told about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T10:32:27-08:00","id":1268328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268223#post1268223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aw man.<br /> <br /> Maybe... its weaker against essence users? I just wanted to make it so that one can actually visualize the maze.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keep working on it, as I mentioned. Big fan of the idea, but not of the implementation. Can't think of a good (in my opinion) implementation from the top of my head, but doesnt mean there isint one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T20:36:26-08:00","id":1268467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268326#post1268326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, how about this?<br /> <br /> The Tell-Tale Shade<br /> Cost: Ritual, 3wp<br /> Duration: Until Sunrise<br /> <br /> Using a link to their target, the sorcerer creates a shade of essence and darkness. This shade is not a spirit, but a simple mimicry of who the link belong to. It can only be ordered by the sorcerer to stay, follow or tell a tale. It wont attack or otherwise help the sorcerer and a single point of damage witch effect spirits destroy it. When it is created, the sorcerer roll (Occult+intelligence) where the successes are the number of tales it can tell before fading.<br /> <br /> The tales the shade tell are of the memories of the target. The sorcerer can specify a specific event (the day you were wed) or a time and date. Typically, only the more memorable moments are told but if the memory is recent (less than a year) the sorcerer can specify to know mundane things (what did you eat for breakfast 23 days ago?)<br /> <br /> At sunrise, the shade fades away along with the link and any remaining tales. During calibration, the shade lasts until calibration is over.<br /> <br /> People who are already dead can be the target of this spell but they tend to forget about the day of their death. Someone who has been a target of this spell can't be made a target again until next month except during calibration.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer who know Tell-Tale Shade as her control spell may choose to experience the memories rather than being told about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>..... hmm.... <br /> <br /> I still want a puppet that can talk. <br /> <br /> Maybe we can simply have it only be able to talk in generalities? &quot;have you accepted bribes?&quot;, &quot;have you commited murder or rape?&quot; or &quot;Are you an exalted?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T07:59:00-08:00","id":1268547,"title":"","content":"Those don't sound like generalities to me. &quot;Murder&quot; is actually a pretty specific thing, for instance, requiring that you intend to kill, that you then follow through with it, <i>and</i> that the living thing you kill is a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-18-2018, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T08:55:43-08:00","id":1268556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268547#post1268547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those don't sound like generalities to me. &amp;quot;Murder&amp;quot; is actually a pretty specific thing, for instance, requiring that you intend to kill, that you then follow through with it, <i>and</i> that the living thing you kill is a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn it. Forget it, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T19:35:38-08:00","id":1268696,"title":"","content":"Question. What about magic for urban environments?<br /> <br /> I've been thinking of a version fo army of the wild that allows control of machines. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T21:59:11-08:00","id":1268724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268696#post1268696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking of a version fo army of the wild that allows control of machines. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) What constitutes a &quot;machine?&quot;<br /> 2) Does the extent of your control go beyond the normal capabilities of the machine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T00:19:03-08:00","id":1268751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268724#post1268724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) What constitutes a &quot;machine?&quot;<br /> 2) Does the extent of your control go beyond the normal capabilities of the machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pulleys, carts, cars, and computers. <br /> <br /> What do you mean by that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T01:38:55-08:00","id":1268760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268751#post1268751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pulleys, carts, cars, and computers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so this is more for a modern game?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268751#post1268751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you cast this spell and command a flip-phone to &quot;attack&quot; me, is it going to yank its charger out of the wall and whip me to death with it, or is it just going to vibrate itself to the edge of the table and hopefully drop onto my foot? <br /> <br /> If you cast it on a car that's out of gas and order it to kill me, will it be able to do more than shift into neutral and hope I am eventually downslope from it so it can roll over me?<br /> <br /> For that matter, how do the machines tell where I am to target me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-19-2018, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T02:06:59-08:00","id":1268767,"title":"","content":"Modern. <br /> <br /> Urm... no they can't do anything. <br /> <br /> I&quot;m more thinking on the havoc that would happen if you suddenly assumed direct control of every single microchip around you in a mile's radius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T02:39:06-08:00","id":1268768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268767#post1268767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urm... no they can't do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, then - this doesn't sound like it'd be terribly useful for pulleys or carts, so why'd you include them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268767#post1268767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I&quot;m more thinking on the havoc that would happen if you suddenly assumed direct control of every single microchip around you in a mile's radius.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, again, this is gonna vary based on what you feel like control should do, and given that you already said they can't do things they can't normally, I'm curious as to what options this leaves you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-19-2018, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T02:59:37-08:00","id":1268774,"title":"","content":"*puts head in hands*<br /> <br /> Fine. No need for power. As long as there's a hinge or socket, they can move. Carts and cars can move under their own power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T03:12:41-08:00","id":1268777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1268696#post1268696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. What about magic for urban environments?<br /> <br /> I've been thinking of a version fo army of the wild that allows control of machines. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Army of the wild's primariy utility is making a battle group--however, given you mention seizing control of microchips, that...seems less like what your going for. I see 2 approaches for designing the spell:<br /> 1-Surreal as all hell<br /> <br /> You seize control of the local technological devices--cars, computers, traffic lights, cellphones, coffee machines, atms--and they become a battle group. In this case, the machines individually are under your control adn you can mess with them (the ATM still deposits money), but they can also serve as the Army of the Wild's typical purchase (go watch Maximum Overdrive for an idea of how that works here). Your machinery is primarily a fighting force--you can't use the ATM to empty an entire nations bank account into your credit account, but you could take all the money or have it rapid fire quarters at people.<br /> <br /> 2-Less Sureal, More Utility<br /> <br /> A more complicated spell would only allow control of the objects. In this case, you would have total control of the utilities of a machine--but you'd want to break down effects into &quot;types&quot; of machines. I.E. you can do X with communications, Y with transport, etc. This would be a spell were you bank and spend successes on a roll I think. This could include things like &quot;Transfer all the money from people in this bank into my bank&quot; or &quot;send out robo calls from every cellphone in a mile&quot; or &quot;use computers to doxx my opponents across the globe&quot; or the like. Things machines are _technically_ capabale of but would require absoulte access to their information and lots of cordination.<br /> <br /> I'm unsure which would be preferable to you, but either appraoch could work in a modern game. I'd go with #1 personally--maybe extend it to allow you to make golems out of the copper wire in buildings, etc. But the 2nd route is doable as well, it just needs some leg work in defining types of tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T00:51:30-08:00","id":1269147,"title":"","content":"Huh. Ok. <br /> <br /> So. Let's say you have a tree that constantly grows fruits. And replaced the fruits within minutes. <br /> <br /> Terrestrial spell? Or celestial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T01:01:16-08:00","id":1269149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1269147#post1269147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Let's say you have a tree that constantly grows fruits. And replaced the fruits within minutes. <br /> <br /> Terrestrial spell? Or celestial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Summoning the Harvest back in 2e was Terrestrial, but you had a limit on how often you could use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T02:05:44-08:00","id":1269154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1269149#post1269149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summoning the Harvest back in 2e was Terrestrial, but you had a limit on how often you could use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. So how about instead of making food by causing an entire field to ripen at once, you have one tree giving a constant supply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T02:27:00-08:00","id":1269156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1269154#post1269154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. So how about instead of making food by causing an entire field to ripen at once, you have one tree giving a constant supply?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I'd do that, because that sort of thing doesn't really seem in the bailiwick for sorcery spells; if she could <i>with one spell</i> make a tree give out an infinite supply of food forever regardless of conditions, why would a sorceress ever take Summoning the Harvest, Food from the Aerial Table, or even Benediction of Archgenesis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T02:53:35-08:00","id":1269162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1269156#post1269156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that I'd do that, because that sort of thing doesn't really seem in the bailiwick for sorcery spells; if she could <i>with one spell</i> make a tree give out an infinite supply of food forever regardless of conditions, why would a sorceress ever take Summoning the Harvest, Food from the Aerial Table, or even Benediction of Archgenesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there'll be limitations. Like time. Or rate of regeneration. Or speed food is produced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T03:28:38-08:00","id":1269168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1269162#post1269162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course there'll be limitations. Like time. Or rate of regeneration. Or speed food is produced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, I was exaggerating - but the quantities of food your spell would produce might as well be infinite.<br /> <br /> Depending on too many factors to get into here, a single modern apple tree can typically produce 20-200 kg of apples in a growing season. We're talking hundreds, to thousands of apples. <br /> <br /> If an apple tree magically replenished its supply of apples every minute, or even every five minutes, you could outpace entire orchards in less than a day. And that's during the growing season. Considering that your proposed spell has it produce &quot;constantly,&quot; a sorcerer who goes place to place casting it will basically render hunger into a thing of the past for Creation.<br /> <br /> So, no, neither Terrestrial nor Celestial seems appropriate. It could work as a Working, but not as a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-20-2018, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T03:30:45-08:00","id":1269169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1269168#post1269168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, I was exaggerating - but the quantities of food your spell would produce might as well be infinite.<br /> <br /> Depending on too many factors to get into here, a single modern apple tree can typically produce 20-200 kg of apples in a growing season. We're talking hundreds, to thousands of apples. <br /> <br /> If an apple tree magically replenished its supply of apples every minute, or even every five minutes, you could outpace entire orchards in less than a day. And that's during the growing season. Considering that your proposed spell has it produce &amp;quot;constantly,&amp;quot; a sorcerer who goes around casting it will basically render hunger into a thing of the past for Creation.<br /> <br /> So, no, neither Terrestrial nor Celestial seems appropriate. It could work as a Working, but not as a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T10:50:37-08:00","id":1270144,"title":"","content":"How about a spell that carries out mass terraforming. I.e. transmutes the very ground into something else. Soil becomes granite. Deserts become fertile soil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T11:26:21-08:00","id":1270155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1270144#post1270144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a spell that carries out mass terraforming. I.e. transmutes the very ground into something else. Soil becomes granite. Deserts become fertile soil</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like workings.And there is a spell that turn deserts fertile, Benediction of archgenesis. I have already mentioned this spell to you before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T12:07:55-08:00","id":1270165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1270155#post1270155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds like workings.And there is a spell that turn deserts fertile, Benediction of archgenesis. I have already mentioned this spell to you before.</div> </div> </div> </div>But benediction of archgenesis is much, much larger. It alters climate, summons animals, makes plants, and is permannet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T01:27:13-08:00","id":1270552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1270165#post1270165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But benediction of archgenesis is much, much larger. It alters climate, summons animals, makes plants, and is permannet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You said nothing about the size of your spell so how can you say wether it is larger or smaller? Same with duration. And while the spell covers a large area, it can only be used once per story.<br /> <br /> You are asking for a spell that can do an important part of a solar level spell can (turn infertile ground into fertile soil) plus extra (transmuting ground into &quot;something else&quot;). You need to be way more specific. For all I know, you can use the spell to turn stone into gold or jade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T02:44:49-08:00","id":1270558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1270552#post1270552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You said nothing about the size of your spell so how can you say wether it is larger or smaller? Same with duration. And while the spell covers a large area, it can only be used once per story.<br /> <br /> You are asking for a spell that can do an important part of a solar level spell can (turn infertile ground into fertile soil) plus extra (transmuting ground into &quot;something else&quot;). You need to be way more specific. For all I know, you can use the spell to turn stone into gold or jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The radius is five miles. The depth is 10 meters. The ground can be transmuted into any other form of ground, as long as the sorcerer knows of it (i.e. has a description of it) or has a sample of it. (if she has a sample of iron ore, she can transform the entire ground into it. No magical materials allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T05:35:12-08:00","id":1270573,"title":"","content":"Which reminds me. There are wide-scale combat defensive buffs. Like, impenetratable frost barrier, burning eyes of the offender, and curtain of quartz. What about offensive buffs, like all ranged attacks explode with the force of grenades, or increased accuracy for all attacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T06:12:02-08:00","id":1270577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1270573#post1270573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which reminds me. There are wide-scale combat defensive buffs. Like, impenetratable frost barrier, burning eyes of the offender, and curtain of quartz.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't just boosts to numbers, though - they achieve their defensive benefits by giving you a fearsome mien, placing barriers, et cetera. I wouldn't have a spell <i>just</i> raise people's Accuracy, since<br /> <br /> 1) Accuracy is an abstract number for the players, and <br /> <br /> 2) What would that even look like, besides one side of the conflict just suddenly hitting more?<br /> <br /> (I'd also be reluctant to permit such a spell because it makes Decisive attacks way more dangerous.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T09:30:07-08:00","id":1270620,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Hungry scream of the blood-thirsty missile</b></i><br /> <br /> The sorcerer speaks the word of prey tracking and sends her mind towards the missiles and ranged weapons of her and her companions, up to Size (occult) people. The ranged weapons and munitions began to let out a screeching noise and glow red, obviating stealth. From now on, any and all ranged weapons used are considered to be enhanced by the spell. <br /> <br /> The spell makes the arrows personally track down and search for prey to destroy, allowing them to ignore cover/ environmental penalties, and to add the sorcerer's occult score in terms of successes/ dice to hit the prey. As they scream in triumph and rage through the atmosphere, they leave behind a crimson trail connecting the weapon and the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T08:55:55-08:00","id":1270845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1270620#post1270620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Hungry scream of the blood-thirsty missile</b></i><br /> <br /> The sorcerer speaks the word of prey tracking and sends her mind towards the missiles and ranged weapons of her and her companions, up to Size (occult) people. The ranged weapons and munitions began to let out a screeching noise and glow red, obviating stealth. From now on, any and all ranged weapons used are considered to be enhanced by the spell.<br /> <br /> The spell makes the arrows personally track down and search for prey to destroy, allowing them to ignore cover/ environmental penalties, and to add the sorcerer's occult score in terms of successes/ dice to hit the prey. As they scream in triumph and rage through the atmosphere, they leave behind a crimson trail connecting the weapon and the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a waste of good fluff for it to simply make the boring effect of easier to hit. It also seem crazy strong at first glance, witch of course depends on cost, duration and circle. Consider giving the BG might 1 and some other special and interesting effect instead maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T19:35:00-08:00","id":1271018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1270845#post1270845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like a waste of good fluff for it to simply make the boring effect of easier to hit. It also seem crazy strong at first glance, witch of course depends on cost, duration and circle. Consider giving the BG might 1 and some other special and interesting effect instead maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I know. But what good effect? The arrows hit and explode like grenades, giving fire damage and aoe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T11:53:14-08:00","id":1271814,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Conjuring the gaze of the Unconquered Sun</b></i><br /> <br /> Sorcery can never affect the Heavens. Those are beneath the purview of the Incarnae. But this doesn't meant that they cannot imitate a small fraction of their power. <br /> <br /> The sorcerer chants the word the rooster sings as the sun appears over the horizon each day. And within the palm of her hand, appears a miniature sun. Then she throws it into the air, and it floats there, the light penetrating all solid materials up to long range. Within that range, it is as if that portion of the world is exposed to the noonday sun, along with all its penalties. Servants of darkness suffer, while ghosts and beings of the underworld begin to dissipate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T11:29:14-08:00","id":1272019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1271814#post1271814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Conjuring the gaze of the Unconquered Sun</b></i><br /> <br /> Sorcery can never affect the Heavens. Those are beneath the purview of the Incarnae. But this doesn't meant that they cannot imitate a small fraction of their power.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer chants the word the rooster sings as the sun appears over the horizon each day. And within the palm of her hand, appears a miniature sun. Then she throws it into the air, and it floats there, the light penetrating all solid materials up to long range. Within that range, it is as if that portion of the world is exposed to the noonday sun, along with all its penalties. Servants of darkness suffer, while ghosts and beings of the underworld begin to dissipate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like it. Needs more details of course. I would beef it up a bit and place it as celestial to keep it out of mortal hands. Unless you want to use it as a plot hook for a mortal faking being a solar (for some reason)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T21:53:34-08:00","id":1272122,"title":"","content":"Why keep it out of mortal hands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T10:04:59-08:00","id":1272198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carrot Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1272019#post1272019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like it. Needs more details of course. I would beef it up a bit and place it as celestial to keep it out of mortal hands. Unless you want to use it as a plot hook for a mortal faking being a solar (for some reason)</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyway, why would I want to place it as celestial? <br /> <br /> In fact, I think its not powerful enough for a terrestrial spell. For goodness sake, this is a circle that includes things like death by obsidian butterflies and an artillery spell that outranges napoleonic cannons. In fact, I think this needs to be wider range, and actually give penalties equal to the sorcerer's occult score, in addition to the damage by sunlight. Oh yeah. And the spell lasts for an entire day. And you can selectively make it so that your own pet demons aren't affected. <br /> <br /> suck it, creatures of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T02:51:42-08:00","id":1272346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1272198#post1272198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, why would I want to place it as celestial?<br /> <br /> In fact, I think its not powerful enough for a terrestrial spell. For goodness sake, this is a circle that includes things like death by obsidian butterflies and an artillery spell that outranges napoleonic cannons. In fact, I think this needs to be wider range, and actually give penalties equal to the sorcerer's occult score, in addition to the damage by sunlight. Oh yeah. And the spell lasts for an entire day. And you can selectively make it so that your own pet demons aren't affected.<br /> <br /> suck it, creatures of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I think it should be celestial is mostly thematic. You need celestial power to call upon the celestial. Balance wise, you could make it work as either depending on the desired effect.<br /> <br /> Though it sounds more fitting in general as a capstone occult charm or evocations for an orichalcum artifact. Does not mean it CAN'T be a spell, but more suitable as other things.<br /> <br /> If you want it to last a day, it should be a ritual. Maybe having it as a controll spell let you cast it as a ritual taking 10 minutes witch last a day but normally it costs sorcerous motes and lasts the scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15748-carrot-crusader","name":"Carrot Crusader","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T06:05:45-08:00","id":1272368,"title":"","content":"Eh.. you can always make a mist of salt and holy water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T06:26:28-08:00","id":1272373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1272368#post1272368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh.. you can always make a mist of salt and holy water.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Holy water&quot; hasn't really been a thing in Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T06:47:01-08:00","id":1272378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1272198#post1272198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, why would I want to place it as celestial?<br /> <br /> In fact, I think its not powerful enough for a terrestrial spell. For goodness sake, this is a circle that includes things like death by obsidian butterflies and an artillery spell that outranges napoleonic cannons. In fact, I think this needs to be wider range, and actually give penalties equal to the sorcerer's occult score, in addition to the damage by sunlight. Oh yeah. And the spell lasts for an entire day. And you can selectively make it so that your own pet demons aren't affected.<br /> <br /> suck it, creatures of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Making it damage creatures of darkness from the start is a good move--i don't beleive creatures of darkness are actually hurt by the sun this addition. <br /> I'd say making it selective or expanding the duration work for controls. <br /> <br /> As for compared to Flight of the Brilliant Raptor or Obsidian Butterflies, I think this spell could be Terrestrial circle...but needs to either be focused on the utility of being a small sun or on being an anti-creature of darkness spell. Kinda reminds me of the fake moons in DBZ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T08:55:41-08:00","id":1272633,"title":"","content":"Hmm..... question. I've been thinking of thaumaturgy. Maybe a spell for each type of creature? Mortal, demon, dead, fae, god, or otherwise?<br /> <br /> Question. Sorcery enhancing battle groups. How much can it go for terrestrial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T10:28:18-08:00","id":1272649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1272633#post1272633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm..... question. I've been thinking of thaumaturgy. Maybe a spell for each type of creature? Mortal, demon, dead, fae, god, or otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy doesn't have spells. Also, I don't feel that, for example, Exorcism, really needs to have a version that works on mortals, since mortals can't dematerialize and possess someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T10:46:47-08:00","id":1272653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1272649#post1272649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgy doesn't have spells. Also, I don't feel that, for example, Exorcism, really needs to have a version that works on mortals, since mortals can't dematerialize and possess someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Sorry. Remember greater ward? That can ward against specific effects and creatures?<br /> <br /> We need some thing along that line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T10:52:48-08:00","id":1272657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1272653#post1272653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. Sorry. Remember greater ward? That can ward against specific effects and creatures?<br /> <br /> We need some thing along that line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we, though? Again, why do we need to ward off mortals?<br /> <br /> Also, this strikes me as one of those things that can be a problem if it's supposed to have a version of itself for everything out there. There are critters that don't readily fit into categories this time around. Things that are dead that aren't ghosts, things that are Wyld that aren't Raksha, things that are beasts that aren't animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-03-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T11:03:27-08:00","id":1272660,"title":"","content":"Fine. Forget the mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T12:19:05-08:00","id":1272669,"title":"","content":"Well, the other issue is that thaumaturgy isn't just a set of folk rituals that any determined hopeful can learn from a book anymore. If there's a ritual to shut out demons from a house, and a separate one that wards out gods, a thaumaturge who isn't already blessed with either will have to go find other thaumaturges who are, and convince them to teach her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T15:07:49-08:00","id":1272711,"title":"","content":"You know what? Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T01:35:14-08:00","id":1272944,"title":"","content":"Ok. Guys? I got an idea. Remember how in xianxia, the more metaphysically powerful you get, the better looking you become?<br /> <br /> How about a spell that temporarily boosts stats and gives a few merits, for a limited amount of time?<br /> <br /> Can work as a weird healing spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T01:55:36-08:00","id":1274156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1272669#post1272669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the other issue is that thaumaturgy isn't just a set of folk rituals that any determined hopeful can learn from a book anymore. If there's a ritual to shut out demons from a house, and a separate one that wards out gods, a thaumaturge who isn't already blessed with either will have to go find other thaumaturges who are, and convince them to teach her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally. A computer. No, that wasn't what I meant. I meant a spell that temporarily blasts out debuffs against a particular type of creature within an area. For example, the earlier sun example took out creatures of darkness and demons. What about one of the green sun, that weakened and sickened the rebellious gods? What about a black moon, that caused illness within all living creatures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T06:23:51-08:00","id":1285868,"title":"","content":"Urgh. Ok. After a long sabbatical...<br /> <br /> Summoning the Riches of the Earth<br /> <br /> The sorcerer makes a symbol that is a combination of the Mudra of the Earth and Wealth, and beckons them to come towards him. Within *, all mineral wealth comes within the radius is pulled towards him and attracted. Gold, silver, iron ore, crystal, any kind, popping out of the earth itself. This can only pull out wealth native to the earth. A bar of gold hidden right under his feet will not be summoned, neither would a stash of silver coins. Additionally, this can never summon the magical materials. Alternatively, he can select a certain criteria, and summon them**, expanding the area to *** and having them pop out. This can only be done in the same area once per year. <br /> <br /> Regenerating the blessings of Stone <br /> <br /> The sorcerer picks up a native stone, and then writes down the sign the gods of heaven write in their forms, when spring begins. And then he buries the stone. For the next day and night, the earth itself rumbles softly. Mining shafts collapse. Soil and dirt expands and multiples itself. Mineral nodes grow. By morning, it is finished. The earth is renewed, and ready to be mined. The spell has two uses: <br /> <br /> 1. It can regenerate the mineral wealth of any area. If it had been mined before, the place will be restored, as if the mines itself had not been set up, and the old prospectors will find veins in the exact same spot.<br /> <br /> 2. It can expand the mineral wealth. Where there was once trace veins of silver, now you can find entire blocks of them the size of your forearm. Where there was enough jewels and gems to fill several crates, one can now bring entire cartloads of them. Where one has enough iron to outfit a battalion, one can now outfit and entire army. <br /> <br /> Same as before. This can be only done the same area once per year. It is incompatible with Summoning the Riches of the Earth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T05:30:09-08:00","id":1293281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/pub?id=1jmxwx7FPXA-jzWJiv2fyCGeJQGQu2QomFTs5j45mPec#h.3yh5nqas9x5e\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/pub?id=1jmxwx7FPXA-jzWJiv2fyCGeJQGQu2QomFTs5j45mPec#h.3yh5nqas9x5e\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/pub?id=1jmxwx7FPXA-jzWJiv2fyCGeJQGQu2QomFTs5j45mPec#h.3yh5nqas9x5e\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/pub?id=1jmxwx7FPXA-jzWJiv2fyCGeJQGQu2QomFTs5j45mPec#h.3yh5nqas9x5e </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hey. An idea:<br /> <br /> Water Dragon's Arrow Cascade<br /> Cost: 15m<br /> <br /> Target: Conjured automaton<br /> <br /> <br /> Just as the Elemental Dragon of Water does not rest solely in the oceans, so too may a sorcerer let deadly water fall upon his foe. This spell requires that the sorcerer have a bow in hand, and, while holding it, make the Sign of Liquidity Dismissed, the mudra made by the small gods who regulate evaporation. Once this is done, they draw an arrow, which glows a midnight blue, and fire it into the sky. Rather than rise forever, however, it lodges in the air 20 yards above the ground, and disintegrates, forming a vaguely feminine, vaguely cephalopodian figure in the sky made of rainwater and blue light. Rainbow bows in her many tentacle-like hands, she salutes the sorcerer once, then begins to pour arrows made of rain down on the sorcerer's foes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Arrow Cascade Maiden understands complex instructions, and has an infinite supply of her rain arrows for her rainbow bows. The dark blue light she emits invalidates her Stealth like a 8-10 mote anima banner, unless it is raining, whereupon the light is quenched. She, as an innate property, applies her Archery-based attacks against five separate targets (or one Mass Combat Unit five times), rolling only once and comparing that to their DVs, but may not flurry them with any other action, for this takes her full concentration. Her arrows of rain have the stats of Broadhead arrows, and her rainbow bows are statted as composite bows (included in her stat-line below). She can fly, as if she had the Wings Abomination, and if engaged up close, will attempt to grapple her foe with her tendril-like arms. The Arrow Cascade Maiden disintegrates if she comes within two yards of the ground, the Essence of Earth absorbing her. Otherwise, the spell ends after 7 hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> This spell can only be countered during casting. Once the maiden appears, only killing her gets rid of her. When the duration of the spell ends, or the maiden is killed, she disintegrates in a heavy, but brief rainstorm with a 100 yard radius, which lasts one long tick, causing appropriate environmental penalties. In times of drought, sorcerers who know this spell have been known to summon Arrow Cascade Maidens just for this purpose.<br /> <br /> <br /> The adepts of Kimbery would disagree that this spell has its roots in Immaculate Teachings, though; this act of sorcery has older, and darker origins. To them, it is known as Loving Mother's Skysent Gifts. This variant of the spell can only make three attacks per action, but the rain-arrows are vitriolic and burning. Any targets which suffer damage from the attacks are affected by a Poison with the stats of Arrow-Frog Venom.<br /> <br /> <br /> Arrow Cascade Maiden<br /> <br /> <br /> Motivation: To puncture the hearts of her sorcerer's foes with her arrows<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2, Charisma 3, Manipulation 1, Appearance 3, Perception 5, Intelligence 2, Wits 4<br /> <br /> Virtues: Automaton: Never fails Valour checks, never makes others<br /> <br /> Abilities: Athletics 3, Awareness 4, Dodge 4, Archery 5 (Rainbow bows +1, Against People With Unarmoured Torsos +2), Presence 4 (Striking Fear Into The Hearts Of Her Summoner's Foes +1), Martial Arts 1 (Clinching +3), Stealth 0 (In The Rain +3), War 3 (Against Those Who Cannot Strike Back Against Her +2)<br /> <br /> Join Battle: 7<br /> <br /> Attacks:<br /> <br /> Rainbow Bow Cascade: Speed 6, Accuracy 10, Damage +6L, Rate 1, Range 300 yards, Tags B<br /> <br /> Clinch: Speed 6, Accuracy 8, Damage +0B, Defence -, Rate 1, Tags C, N, P<br /> <br /> Soak: 5L/5B (Rain-nature 4L/2B)<br /> <br /> Health Levels: -0/-1/-1/-2/-2/-4/Incap<br /> <br /> Dodge DV: 4 Willpower: 10 (0 against sorcerer)<br /> <br /> Essence: 1<br /> <br /> Other Notes: Unless given orders to the contrary, an Arrow Cascade Maiden will always aim to get the maximum possible benefit, and will preferentially target anyone who wears armour which does not cover the chest properly or who lacks armour there entirely, the better that her arrows seek out the hearts of her master's foes. In a rainstorm, she will attempt to reestablish surprise, and conceal where her arrows are coming from among the rain.<br /> <br /> What about construction of servitors and turrets? Like starcraft turrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T02:42:28-07:00","id":1296635,"title":"","content":"The eye, the mouth, and the ear - terrestrial spell<br /> (20sm, 1wp)<br /> <br /> The sorcerer conjures up a metallic head, a cariacuture of a bust. The surface has a metallic shine, and it has one mouth, one eye, and one ear.<br /> <br /> Upon speaking the word of Farsight, the eye and ear flies off and dematerialises, while the mouth opens wide and a picture is conjured in its maw. What the eyes sees is displayed, and what the ear hears is repriduced by the mouth.<br /> <br /> The eye and ear can turn immaterial, capable of moving through solid stone and steel. They create a soft tinkling sound as the move, and the air shimmers with their presence. A sharp eyed or eared observer can detect these signs, and potentially destroy them. The eye and ear only turn immaterial when moving through obstacles. They can be destroyed easily, holding only one health level.<br /> <br /> The range of the eye and ear is approximately 1 mile + sorcerer's occult score. Their top speed is 40miles per hour, and are immune to environmental hazards.<br /> <br /> The head itself can record up to 1 hr of sound and video. <br /> <br /> *an Internet cookie to whoever gets this reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T02:46:43-07:00","id":1296636,"title":"","content":"There's already a spell called the Eye and the Mouth, it's just a translation spell basically.<br /> <br /> Also, do you expect this to be used in combat? It must be hard to focus on the sensory input when you're still having to dodge attacks. I would just have it be a ritual spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-14-2019, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T02:59:11-07:00","id":1296638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1296636#post1296636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's already a spell called the Eye and the Mouth, it's just a translation spell basically.<br /> <br /> Also, do you expect this to be used in combat? It must be hard to focus on the sensory input when you're still having to dodge attacks. I would just have it be a ritual spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man. <br /> <br /> Seems I wrote it wrongly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T10:58:55-07:00","id":1296746,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Eye, The Mouth, and the Ear<br /> (Ritual, 1wp)</b></span><br /> <br /> The sorcerer chants the words of the all-seeing and all-hearing. In flash of light, a piece of metal shaped like a head appears in his hand. The surface is blue-grey, and the metal bst has one mouth, one eye, and one ear. Upon speaking the word of Farsight, the eye and ear fly off and dematerialises, while the mouth expands and begins to depict images seen by the eye, and reproduce sounds heard by the ear. The eye and ear can travel through walls and obstacles, but it does not protect them from being attacked, except by environmental hazards. Their passage through the world leaves a soft tinkling of silver bells and a faint shimmer. One with sharp senses can hear this, and destroy them, protecting them from eavesdropping. <br /> <br /> The eye and ear are intelligent, and can follow basic orders, such as 'follow this man' or 'next person to enter the building is to be followed' or 'find the man inside with a red coat, and watch him as he converses with the man with a black hat'. The mouth is capable of storing up to an hour of video and sound. <br /> <br /> If the eye and ear are destroyed, it takes one day for the mouth to regenerate them. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Eye and ear: </b></span><br /> <br /> Essence 1<br /> Automaton<br /> <br /> Attributes: Dexterity 4, Perception 5, Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Strength 1<br /> Abilities: Athletics 4 (only for flying), Stealth 3 (In the corner +3), Awareness 5 (Sight +3), Investigation 2<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> <b>Sharp eye</b>: The eye is capable of bypassing environmental effects such as darkness, mist, dust, or fog. It sees just as well in the deep ocean or mists as the clear blue sky. If blocked by something substantial, like wood or stone, it rolls to penetrate it<br /> <br /> <b>Discerning ear</b>: The ear is capable of picking out voices amongst a crowded carnival, a pin dropping in a noisy bazaar, as long as it knows what its looking for<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *an Internet cookie to whoever gets this reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T16:17:05-07:00","id":1296818,"title":"","content":"What happens when it's your control spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T16:45:13-07:00","id":1296821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1296818#post1296818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when it's your control spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I'm thinking of either an increase in range, or being capable of making more. <br /> <br /> Actually, yeah, that's something I left out. You can only make one at a time. And I'm not sure on how intelligent I should make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T02:33:18-07:00","id":1322724,"title":"","content":"So I've been looking at Conan again. <br /> <br /> What bonuses should you get for, say, making a human sacrifice? As a component of a spell? <br /> <br /> Also, I think that on the healing sorcery, I have an idea. Abe no Seimei, once made a... doll. To take his place, in death. When the grim reaper came, he took the doll, instead of the sorcerer. How about a spell that lets you 'push' injuries and maladies onto another person, based upon occult score? <br /> <br /> Or is that too much like sorcerous workings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T02:42:46-07:00","id":1322729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1322724#post1322724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been looking at Conan again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one? The short stories by Robert E. Howard, the movies with Arnold Schwarzenegger, the Marvel comics?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1322724#post1322724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What bonuses should you get for, say, making a human sacrifice? As a component of a spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the spell and your initiation obviously. For instance, the Core has the Pact with an Ifrit Lord initiation that lets you make sacrifices for sorcerous motes. But by default <i>most spells</i> aren't going to be aided by killing someone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1322724#post1322724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think that on the healing sorcery, I have an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which healing sorcery?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1322724#post1322724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abe no Seimei, once made a... doll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who? I don't remember him in any Conan stories...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah, okay, the Japanese folklore guy. Okay. Nothing to do with Conan at all, then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1322724#post1322724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a spell that lets you 'push' injuries and maladies onto another person, based upon occult score?<br /> <br /> Or is that too much like sorcerous workings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be inclined to make it a sorcerous working, myself, as it doesn't seem like something one should be expected to do regularly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-07-2019, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T03:36:46-07:00","id":1322737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1322729#post1322729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which one? The short stories by Robert E. Howard, the movies with Arnold Schwarzenegger, the Marvel comics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I mean the conan rpg. <br /> <br /> There are quite a lot of fascinating stuff. There's a spell which rips out your opponents' eyeballs. Then there's another that leaves your victim a withered husk that experiences excrutiating pain for the rest of their existence. Which if they are not destroyed by a 3rd party, is forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T14:01:35-07:00","id":1344063,"title":"","content":"So I guess this is the thread for custom sorcery spells? I was going to just post in the Sorcerous Workings thread, but if nobody minds me bumping an older thread then here's an idea I had earlier.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I was originally thinking of more interesting ways to produce food than Food From the Aerial Table, and I ended up with this weird concept. The original idea was something like &quot;what if you used a sorcerous working to give someone an ability similar to the Second Bread thaumaturgy ritual,&quot; but I decided that something too similar to an existing power wasn't a great choice. Hatching animals out of plants was probably vaguely inspired by Odin Sphere.<br /> <br /> <b>Wood Dragon's Clutch</b> (Terrestrial Circle Spell)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> Ritual, 1wp<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> The sorcerer plants a fist-sized &quot;seed&quot; in the earth consisting of one or more body parts from an animal. Any part(s) of the animal will do -- meat, bones, organs, whatever else -- as long as all the material is from one species of creature; the earth need not be suitable for growing normal crops, but it must be at least moist -- even desert sand will do as long as the sorcerer pours water on it. Over the course of an hour, the sorcerer covers the &quot;seed&quot; with earth while reciting a ritual giving of thanks; sorcerers of the First Age gave praise to Gaia for nature's gifts, but Dragon-Blooded sorcerers in the Age of Sorrows give acknowledgement to Sextes Jylis instead.<br /> <br /> During the next five hours, a shrub-like plant grows, eventually producing &quot;fruit&quot; in the form of a clutch of eggs. Each egg hatches into a healthy juvenile (not newborn) member of the species that originally gave rise to the new plant; they are generally typical examples of the species, and have enough instinctive knowledge to take care of themselves if left to their own devices, but no special training. The new animals hatch with a Minor Tie of affection towards the sorcerer that grew them, and are unlikely to attack the sorcerer or his associates in the short term, but the Tie is not guaranteed to last -- an unprepared sorcerer who is not skilled in animal husbandry might very well see his creations disperse into the wild depending on their temperament.<br /> <br /> The number of eggs produced depends on the size of the animal in question:<br /> - An animal the size of a quail, dove, or other small bird yields (sorcerer's Essence * 4) eggs<br /> - An animal the size of a chicken, duck, turkey, or large rat yields (sorcerer's Essence * 2) eggs<br /> - An animal the size of a sheep, goat, or small pony yields (sorcerer's Essence) eggs<br /> - An animal the size of a horse, cow, bison, or camel yields (sorcerer's Essence)/2 rounded up eggs<br /> - This spell isn't capable of producing creatures with Legendary Size.<br /> - This spell also doesn't work on humans, or on spirits of any sort.<br /> <br /> This spell is not an effective method for breeding high-quality animals. While the hatched animals are not all identical and display some degree of variation, they are not the children of the particular animal(s) who donated the &quot;seed&quot; -- burying the bones of a fine Marukani horse will yield only horses that are more or less average. The spell is more often used to produce animals for food or other farming purposes.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer who knows Wood Dragon's Clutch as her control spell <i>can</i> use the spell for selective breeding -- if she so chooses, the newly hatched animals <i>will</i> be the genetic offspring of the seed's donor(s). This effect is always optional.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Titan-Hatching Seedling</b> (Celestial Circle Spell)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> Ritual, 1wp<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> This spell functions as Wood Dragon's Clutch, but may produce a single creature with Legendary Size (or at least, a single juvenile creature that will have Legendary Size when fully grown). The plant takes seven hours instead of five to grow in this case. A sorcerer with Essence 6+ can hatch a pair of such animals instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T14:55:03-07:00","id":1344075,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Though personally, I'll sub Essence with Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T21:16:35-07:00","id":1344119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344075#post1344075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome. Though personally, I'll sub Essence with Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea. In retrospect, I don't think mortal sorcerers should necessarily be limited to creating only one sheep at a time -- that feels kind of weak, however miraculous the spell itself may be.<br /> <br /> Maybe instead of depending on the sorcerer's traits, it should just be a flat number based on creature size? Two dozen small birds, one dozen chickens, half a dozen sheep, or two cows? (I have no idea what's appropriate, honestly.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T02:28:12-07:00","id":1344156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344119#post1344119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a bad idea. In retrospect, I don't think mortal sorcerers should necessarily be limited to creating only one sheep at a time -- that feels kind of weak, however miraculous the spell itself may be.<br /> <br /> Maybe instead of depending on the sorcerer's traits, it should just be a flat number based on creature size? Two dozen small birds, one dozen chickens, half a dozen sheep, or two cows? (I have no idea what's appropriate, honestly.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... Let's all remember that in an age where most people build their own houses, your sorcerer can have a fancy two story house with a fireplace, attic, and basement. Your sorcerer can have an infinite water supply, conjure water and food, and bring an entire field to crop in just one moment. <br /> <br /> Being able to create half a dozen cows ain't much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T13:05:22-07:00","id":1344241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344156#post1344156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh... Let's all remember that in an age where most people build their own houses, your sorcerer can have a fancy two story house with a fireplace, attic, and basement. Your sorcerer can have an infinite water supply, conjure water and food, and bring an entire field to crop in just one moment.<br /> <br /> Being able to create half a dozen cows ain't much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tell that to the Irish. Or if you prefer an Exalted example, to the Harbourheadites.<br /> <br /> Cows are insanely valuable in pre-industrial societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T13:14:37-07:00","id":1344242,"title":"","content":"No exaggeration: People sometimes <i>killed</i> for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T13:17:16-07:00","id":1344244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344242#post1344242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No exaggeration: People sometimes <i>killed</i> for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Cattle-raids wouldn\u00b4t be raids if there wasn\u00b4t a big chance of violence, sometimes deadly violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T13:18:15-07:00","id":1344245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344241#post1344241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Tell that to the Irish. Or if you prefer an Exalted example, to the Harbourheadites.<br /> <br /> Cows are insanely valuable in pre-industrial societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like how you can make a dozen pregnant cows immediately give birth, skipping months and months of waiting? <br /> <br /> Or how making a baby is considered to be a basic project? <br /> <br /> Normally, you'll be right. But Exalted sorcery is literally biblical. Big, strong, overwhelming effects. Conjuring an animal isn't that crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T13:54:26-07:00","id":1344250,"title":"","content":"That cows are insanely valuable doesn't mean they're not easy to conjure via sorcery if there's a spell specifically for that. By that logic, Artifacts (being insanely valuable, way more than cows) shouldn't be something you could effectively conjure through spells like Wood Dragon's Claws or Invulnerable Skin of Bronze. Having someone be unable to ever speak of something you choose is a power many people would kill and go to war for and yet Corrupted Words exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T17:20:52-07:00","id":1344302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344250#post1344250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That cows are insanely valuable doesn't mean they're not easy to conjure via sorcery if there's a spell specifically for that. By that logic, Artifacts (being insanely valuable, way more than cows) shouldn't be something you could effectively conjure through spells like Wood Dragon's Claws or Invulnerable Skin of Bronze. Having someone be unable to ever speak of something you choose is a power many people would kill and go to war for and yet Corrupted Words exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got any examples of the corrupted words thing? <br /> <br /> Actually, I remember something. I once remember bemoaning 'Army of the Wild''s weaknesses, and made a spell that could let you, out of essence, permanently conjure animals. It was actually so that you could conjure up river dragons and tyrant lizards and throw them at your enemies, but summoning up entire herds of swine and cows should be doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T17:57:30-07:00","id":1344305,"title":"","content":"Examples of it? Like, you could make someone unable to speak of an event that would otherwise cause a court scandal or an exile or w/e, cast it on someone who discovers the nature of the Sidereal Exalted to keep the secret until they finally forget it, impede a commander from explaining his strategy at a council or whatever other applications you could think of for &quot;Cannot ever speak of X topic that can be as broad or narrow as you choose&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T19:38:01-07:00","id":1344326,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think President Trump would be willing to give his left testicle for the Corrupted Words spell right about now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T19:46:46-07:00","id":1344329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344326#post1344326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think President Trump would be willing to give his left testicle for the Corrupted Words spell right about now.</div> </div> </div> </div>He has those? <br /> <br /> *insert laughtrack*<br /> <br /> But enough of that. Currently I'm eyeballing terrestrial sorcery effects as something that should match essence 2/3 solar Charms. Only with additional limitations and a focus on flash effects. Like crack mending technique.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T19:55:12-07:00","id":1344331,"title":"","content":"I honestly wouldn't put an Essence tag on them as much as look at existing effects and compare their overall utility and scope. It's rather easy to notice how they go up as you ascend in Circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T20:16:45-07:00","id":1344334,"title":"","content":"The comparison between sorcery spells and Exalted Charms is hardly so cut-and-dry. The flight granted by Eagle Wing Style is very different from the flight granted by Stormwind Rider or Cirrus Skiff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-28-2019, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T20:20:51-07:00","id":1344335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344334#post1344334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comparison between sorcery spells and Exalted Charms is hardly so cut-and-dry. The flight granted by Eagle Wing Style is very different from the flight granted by Stormwind Rider or Cirrus Skiff.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But both give immense mobility, but put in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T18:31:06-07:00","id":1344548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344156#post1344156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh... Let's all remember that in an age where most people build their own houses, your sorcerer can have a fancy two story house with a fireplace, attic, and basement. Your sorcerer can have an infinite water supply, conjure water and food, and bring an entire field to crop in just one moment.<br /> <br /> Being able to create half a dozen cows ain't much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess if you're going to try and balance spells by economic impact (probably not the best way to balance anything), then the demon-summoning spells are likely to beat any number of mundane animals you could create. A few hopping puppeteers (to give one example) could put a city's worth of masons out of business.<br /> <br /> (The control spell effect could get a bit wild if some Marukani sorcerer starts turning his prize horses into a <i>lot</i> of prize horses, but a sorcerer who's serious about animal breeding could do far crazier shit than that anyway.)<br /> <br /> I'm certainly open to further suggestions if anyone has ideas for a spell of this sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T00:02:24-07:00","id":1344592,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest. It's a thing I've been wondering. A hopping puppetteer according to what I can tell simply counts as 10 men for the purpose of construction. How does it put a city's worth of masons out of business?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T02:16:31-07:00","id":1344616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344245#post1344245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just like how you can make a dozen pregnant cows immediately give birth, skipping months and months of waiting? <br /> <br /> Or how making a baby is considered to be a basic project?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you point me at a page number for these things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T02:21:51-07:00","id":1344617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344616#post1344616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you point me at a page number for these things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page number? <br /> <br /> IIRC, summoning of the harvest lets you either create an entire field of newly grown crops, or make every animal pregnant within several hundred meters to give birth with no complications or issues <br /> <br /> The 'baby being a basic project' is something I heard from someone on reddit. Apparently, they were talking with a dev/ someone, and neomah making a baby counts as a basic project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T03:06:48-07:00","id":1344624,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s magic intrinsic to the Neomah, not necessarily intended to be reflective of the baby-making process for everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T05:09:31-07:00","id":1344635,"title":"","content":"Hmm... <br /> <br /> A thing I just heard. A spell to turn sand and dirt into rice and grain. How should it be statted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T23:15:20-07:00","id":1345172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344635#post1344635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...<br /> <br /> A thing I just heard. A spell to turn sand and dirt into rice and grain. How should it be statted?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's all the spell does, it isn't a terribly powerful effect by Exalted standards -- after all, you still need to cook and distribute the stuff if you're feeding a group of people, and it certainly doesn't make for a healthy diet on its own. (Obviously still valuable if you're dealing with a famine or extreme poverty, of course.) So you should probably get a <i>lot</i> of rice and grain out of this.<br /> <br /> Maybe one casting gives you enough rice and/or grain to feed a battle group of Size (sorcerer's Intelligence) for a day? Or maybe more than one day? I'm having trouble visualizing the quantity of rice involved here.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of a good name for this spell, but nothing comes to mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344592#post1344592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest. It's a thing I've been wondering. A hopping puppeteer according to what I can tell simply counts as 10 men for the purpose of construction. How does it put a city's worth of masons out of business?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I admit that this may have been a bit of an exaggeration (depending on how large the city is), but how many masons does one city need at a given time? A sorcerer could summon a new demon every day until they have as many as needed, in any case. The hard part would be keeping the hopping puppeteers supervised to make sure they stayed on task instead of reshaping something to Yozi aesthetics. (Actually, that might be the mortal masons' new job.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T17:04:05-08:00","id":1345665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1345172#post1345172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's all the spell does, it isn't a terribly powerful effect by Exalted standards -- after all, you still need to cook and distribute the stuff if you're feeding a group of people, and it certainly doesn't make for a healthy diet on its own. (Obviously still valuable if you're dealing with a famine or extreme poverty, of course.) So you should probably get a <i>lot</i> of rice and grain out of this.<br /> <br /> Maybe one casting gives you enough rice and/or grain to feed a battle group of Size (sorcerer's Intelligence) for a day? Or maybe more than one day? I'm having trouble visualizing the quantity of rice involved here.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of a good name for this spell, but nothing comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's easy. Stone to bread. <br /> <br /> I think there should be something for this. Its basically a single spell that goes under the concept of 'turn unvaluble things into food'. It should turn stone to bread, wood to meat, sand and dust into rice and grain. I say that it should be compared to food from the aerial table... <br /> <br /> Which lets you... <br /> <br /> Oh hell, we may as well just compare it to the one from 'book of the Emerald Circle'. It's not like anyone here like the Black and White treatise anyway. <br /> <br /> <b>Curse Machine<br /> cost: 15 motes</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The sorcerer murmurs the words of decay, and visualizes the rusting of metal. And then, he focuses. Either on a machine within (Willpower + Essence) meters close to him, a machine he has a sympathetic connection to, or in the form of a curse that can be applied by touch. Were it to apply by touch, the curse would manifest on his hands, feet, or any other body part, and affects any machine he touches for the rest of the scene. <br /> <br /> The sorcerer rolls Occult + Intelligence, adding his essence in bonus dice. Then the effect is applied onto the machines. The more complex the machine, the more easier it is to break. A simple lightbulb is difficulty 5. A car engine is difficulty 3. A laptop or computer is difficulty 1. The effect depends on the number of extra successes. If the difficulty roll is beaten, the machine simply fails, requiring a maintenance check and repair to be made. An extra success to beat the roll means that they can fatally damage the machine, requiring that it unrepairable and have to be thrown out. 2 extra successes means that they can make the machine fail dangerously. Factory equipment kills and cripples the workmen. A laptop explodes, glass and plastic shredding the body of the user. The engines catch fire and the car skids dangerously, exploding and killing. Even a lightbulb would explode, the glass shards penetrating eyes and throats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T03:20:04-08:00","id":1347207,"title":"","content":"How overpowered would a spell that made your crops grow twice as fast and granted them unnatural vitality be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T03:26:32-08:00","id":1347208,"title":"","content":"Depends on the details, area it covers, etc. But considering how powerful Benediction of Archgenesis is, it doesn't look overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T03:32:20-08:00","id":1347210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1347208#post1347208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the details, area it covers, etc. But considering how powerful Benediction of Archgenesis is, it doesn't look overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more thinking of a companion spell to summoning the harvest. Just slightly bigger.<br /> <br /> Focus is in slow, steady improvement of the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T04:13:20-08:00","id":1347214,"title":"","content":"For reference there's a 4 dot Hearthstone that does exactly that :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Harvest Gem (Greater)<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords: </span>Linked<br /> Any fields within five miles of this stone are exceptionally fertile. On good or average years all crops regularly produce yields more than twice as large as their normal best, and ven in bad years, harvests are equal to the best yields that could normally be produced with the same tools and effort. This stone does not reduce the need for labor or seed, but it guarantees this labor will always be well rewarded. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T04:57:59-08:00","id":1347216,"title":"","content":"Huh. So a support or indiction?..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T07:49:43-08:00","id":1347239,"title":"","content":"A support, I meant to highlight that this kind of effect is completely allowed by the system.<br /> <br /> If I were to make a guess I'd place it somewhere between Terrestrial 3 (can canonically bless or curse a small region to affect how well people can live off of it) and Celestial 2 (can canonically bless a town-sized region to increase the duration of its harvest Season by 1 month).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T18:28:57-08:00","id":1347366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1347239#post1347239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A support, I meant to highlight that this kind of effect is completely allowed by the system.<br /> <br /> If I were to make a guess I'd place it somewhere between Terrestrial 3 (can canonically bless or curse a small region to affect how well people can live off of it) and Celestial 2 (can canonically bless a town-sized region to increase the duration of its harvest Season by 1 month).</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm talking about a terrestrial spell... Not a sorcerous working","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T20:18:50-08:00","id":1347387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1347366#post1347366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I'm talking about a terrestrial spell... Not a sorcerous working</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, got the threads confused there. Spells don't really have months long effects as far as I can tell. A spell to grow crops would likely grow them in a day or less instead of just growing them twice as fast.<br /> <br /> I'd probably put some restriction on how much you can spam the spell (i.e. you can't cast it twice on the same field in the same harvest season), but otherwise it can probably be done just fine as a Terrestrial spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T21:53:23-08:00","id":1347400,"title":"","content":"Thing is, Epitome, that is already a canonical spell. He wants this to be a companion to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T06:00:59-08:00","id":1347458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1347400#post1347400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, Epitome, that is already a canonical spell. He wants this to be a companion to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't know 2e spells so I didn't realize.<br /> <br /> Well then mechanically it doesn't seem overpowered, the only issue I see is that months-long buffs aren't really a thing spells do thematically.<br /> <br /> So you just need to fluff over that. For instance the spell could actually be Summon Elemental with a homebrewed Wood Elemental that basically can do the equivalent of a single use of the spell. Or the spell could create otherworldly farming equipment that withers away after 1 harvest. That sort of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T23:23:53-08:00","id":1347621,"title":"","content":"So I've been thinking. Peacock shadow eyes lets you carry out memory rewriting and instill beliefs and thoughts into someone else. Theft of memory lets you steal memories. Sorcerer's puppetry lets you grab someone's body and use it to stab someone. <br /> <br /> What about a mind break spell? A spell that, if you cast and you manage to beat a roll, the target will, until counterspelled, be susceptible to your commands? It's not that he likes you. It's just that, from his perspective, your 'force of will' or 'your commands' can't be disobeyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T00:00:44-08:00","id":1347626,"title":"","content":"You mean like Threefold Binding of the Heart?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T00:47:24-08:00","id":1347633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1347626#post1347626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean like Threefold Binding of the Heart?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But more subtle. Threefold binding of the heart means that he's your adoring slave. <br /> <br /> This spell means that it's far harder for him to disobey you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T01:23:42-08:00","id":1347635,"title":"","content":"To clarify a bit on how the social system works in 3e - I can't just tell you, &quot;Give me a hundred bucks,&quot; and get to roll for it. For me to get you to do something, I leverage one of your Intimacies in a Persuade roll against your Resolve, or offer you something valuable as part of a Bargain roll against your Resolve, or intimidate you with a Threaten roll against your Resolve. And if you invoke a Decision Point or otherwise resist my influence, I have to present a more compelling argument before I can roll again. Certain magics like Hypnotic Tongue Technique (a potent Presence Charm) allow you to bypass the regular social rules, but even it's got to get past Resolve.<br /> <br /> So can you give us a little more to work with, here?<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-11-2019, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T19:40:45-08:00","id":1348981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1347635#post1347635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify a bit on how the social system works in 3e - I can't just tell you, &amp;quot;Give me a hundred bucks,&amp;quot; and get to roll for it. For me to get you to do something, I leverage one of your Intimacies in a Persuade roll against your Resolve, or offer you something valuable as part of a Bargain roll against your Resolve, or intimidate you with a Threaten roll against your Resolve. And if you invoke a Decision Point or otherwise resist my influence, I have to present a more compelling argument before I can roll again. Certain magics like Hypnotic Tongue Technique (a potent Presence Charm) allow you to bypass the regular social rules, but even it's got to get past Resolve.<br /> <br /> So can you give us a little more to work with, here?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this. There's a kingdom that needs spying. And you need a spy on the inside. Someone who knows the layout. You're here to grab a secretary that knows her shit. <br /> <br /> Basically you're here to hypnotize them. Their own beliefs won't change, but they will follow your instructions. They're still loyal to the regime... They just won't find anything wrong with telling you about state secrets, or once a month dropping off a thumb drive containing classified documents into a preprepared dead drop. Their beliefs aren't changed. It's simply a form of dissonance that they won't notice unless someone points it out to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T19:47:36-08:00","id":1348984,"title":"","content":"That sounds exactly like Hypnotic Tongue Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T21:00:57-08:00","id":1348995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1348984#post1348984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds exactly like Hypnotic Tongue Technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. <br /> <br /> Did I... accidentally step on charm space? I swear, I got it from a fantasy series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T21:44:21-08:00","id":1348998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1348995#post1348995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I... accidentally step on charm space? I swear, I got it from a fantasy series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m just saying that it feels like you\u2019re trying to reinvent the wheel here. HTT is already right there, just use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T21:54:48-08:00","id":1348999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1348998#post1348998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m just saying that it feels like you\u2019re trying to reinvent the wheel here. HTT is already right there, just use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess you're right. <br /> <br /> Ok, one more idea. We know that sorcery is grand. Death by obsidian butterflies lets you clear out battalions, and that firey bird lets you outrange Napoleonic artillery. So here's the thing. What about something with a bit more precision? I'm thinking of a spell that turns the air around you rancid and necrotic, swiftly rotting away flesh and equipment. You send out the poisoned smoke like a snake, and it strikes at your enemies, spreading like fire and avoiding what ever you wish unharmed. It inflicts damage on the level of, say, a lava or acid bath, and causes no collateral damage. It's pure damage potential is not as large as death by obsidian butterflies, nor is it as wide-ranged as Brilliant Raptor, but trapped in an urban environment, it can strike from corners where no one can see, and kill your enemies in cramped and winding spaces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T23:38:55-08:00","id":1349006,"title":"","content":"Sounds reasonable. <br /> <br /> How long does it last? How large of an area can it cover? How fast does it move? What\u2019s the difficulty to resist it?<br /> <br /> I could see this being a Terrestrial or Celestial spell depending on a few factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T00:17:16-08:00","id":1349013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349006#post1349006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> How long does it last? How large of an area can it cover? How fast does it move? What\u2019s the difficulty to resist it?<br /> <br /> I could see this being a Terrestrial or Celestial spell depending on a few factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see..... scene-long, probably not more than a single building. I'm thinking of, say, roughly in 40 metres in range. If you're fast? You can outrun it, but you'll need to be at least olympic in sprinting. Resistance? It's like a lava bath, minus your essence rating. It's basically meant as another way to sweep off hordes of mooks, adapted for cramped urban spaces. You can snap your fingers and blast away mortals and zombies, but things like demons or exalted, they're going to survive it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T00:53:57-08:00","id":1349018,"title":"","content":"Exalted can also be Essence 1, dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T01:17:27-08:00","id":1349022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349018#post1349018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted can also be Essence 1, dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it's some schmuchk who should just die. If you throw death of obsidian butterflies at an Essence 1 Solar, who *checks the charm list* only has durability of oak meditation and dipping swallow defense, then he should either die, or be horribly injured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T01:30:21-08:00","id":1349024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349022#post1349022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it's some schmuchk who should just die. If you throw death of obsidian butterflies at an Essence 1 Solar, who *checks the charm list* only has durability of oak meditation and dipping swallow defense, then he should either die, or be horribly injured.</div> </div> </div> </div>As everyone knows, a fledgling demigod who can overthrow nations and change the course of history is,<br /> of course, some shmuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T01:37:26-08:00","id":1349028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349024#post1349024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As everyone knows, a fledgling demigod who can overthrow nations and change the course of history is,<br /> of course, some shmuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, upon review, just throws two charms is enough to shrug off Death of Obseidan Butterflies a lot of the time, so that comparison doesn\u2019t even make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T02:51:17-08:00","id":1349038,"title":"","content":"Alright, fine. You got me. <br /> <br /> Halve the damage to anyone with an active essence pool. But the lava bath thing still stays. I want the horribly deadly gas to move around and engulf hapless mortals, letting them release one final scream of pain and terror before collapsing into grinning skeletons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T03:21:51-08:00","id":1349042,"title":"","content":"Considering that it\u2019s super-competitive with the Celestial spells Magma Kraken and Torrential Cascade, this sounds like another work of the Sapphire Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T03:24:24-08:00","id":1349043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349042#post1349042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that it\u2019s super-competitive with the Celestial spells Magma Kraken and Torrential Cascade, this sounds like another work of the Sapphire Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you say would bump it down into terrestrial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T05:50:51-08:00","id":1349057,"title":"","content":"A <i>much</i> shorter duration for one. The Terrestrial spell Mists of Eventide creates a cloud of poison that only lasts for a few rounds. Death of Obsidian Butterflies is instantaneous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T06:07:01-08:00","id":1349059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349057#post1349057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A <i>much</i> shorter duration for one. The Terrestrial spell Mists of Eventide creates a cloud of poison that only lasts for a few rounds. Death of Obsidian Butterflies is instantaneous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Snap fingers, and the deadly smog of dust only appears for a few moments before leaving behind skeletons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T07:52:34-08:00","id":1349074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349059#post1349059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snap fingers, and the deadly smog of dust only appears for a few moments before leaving behind skeletons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the rolls manage to kill them, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T07:55:10-08:00","id":1349075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349074#post1349074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the rolls manage to kill them, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe we should just Stat the damage as slightly more than death by Obsidian butterflies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T07:56:39-08:00","id":1349076,"title":"","content":"Right now you have :<br /> <br /> -Terrestrial<br /> -Building Wide<br /> -Perfect Smart Targeting<br /> -No collateral damage whatsoever<br /> -Instant 7L against mortals, 3-4 against exalts<br /> <br /> Balance-wise, the spell could really use some complications/drawbacks, else no one will ever pick obsidian butterflies or brilliant raptor ever again.<br /> <br /> <br /> More importantly, Narrative-wise the spell currently doesn't drive a conflict forward in interesting ways, it's 100% a quest skip mechanic. All the complications of Sorceries are ultimately there to make Sorceries influence battles in more interesting ways than just being <i>the biggest gun</i> in the room. It's why brilliant raptor sets the battlefield on fire, why butterflies leave difficult terrain behind, why the Celestial level &quot;kill all mooks&quot; (Cantata of Empty Voices) is a slow, escapeable buildup of sheer soul-crushing horror, and why all published offensive Sorceries have friendly fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want the effect of killing every mortal enemy in the building to be flawless, then the complication needs to be elsewhere. Some examples :<ul><li>There is a secondary blast zone around the building which kills and destroys things indiscriminately. The size of this zone is not fully under the sorcerer's control (e.g. The more people the spell kills, the larger this zone will be).</li> </ul><ul><li>The mortals that get devoured are fueling the creation of a berserk monstrosity of lava, acid and death, which will spawn inside the building and be stronger the more mortals it killed. It must be stopped rapidly, because it specifically seeks to destroy and kill everything that was spared by the spell.</li> </ul><ul><li>You must gather a group of volunteers (which must include yourself) to serve as alternate sacrifices. Each time the spell would spare someone per your wishes, a volunteer chosen at random is hit by the spell instead. At any point you can choose to stop sparing targets to stop further damage among the volunteers.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T07:58:27-08:00","id":1349077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349075#post1349075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we should just Stat the damage as slightly more than death by Obsidian butterflies.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDeath of Obsidian Butterflies doesn't <i>have</i> a set damage count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T07:01:31-08:00","id":1349329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349077#post1349077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bDeath of Obsidian Butterflies doesn't <i>have</i> a set damage count.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. But there's a mechanic for it right? Make it slightly higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T07:25:30-08:00","id":1349331,"title":"","content":"Okay, but Death of Obsidian Butterflies' variable part comes from the successes on the attack roll; this is an environmental hazard - you don't roll to hit someone with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T07:32:04-08:00","id":1349333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349331#post1349331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but Death of Obsidian Butterflies' variable part comes from the successes on the attack roll; this is an environmental hazard - you don't roll to hit someone with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry then.<br /> <br /> Basically, I want a more targeted, more lethal form of death by Obsidian butterflies. Is that OK?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T07:39:07-08:00","id":1349334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349333#post1349333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I want a more targeted, more lethal form of death by Obsidian butterflies. Is that OK?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to take Accelerator's Killing Cloud as a spell, why would I pick up Death of Obsidian Butterflies after?<br /> <br /> \u200bLike, if you want this to be Terrestrial, what's the downside that stops this from being a technically superior version of DoOB? It's more precise <i>and</i> does more damage <i>and</i> leaves inorganic stuff like money, armor and weapons undamaged for looting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-18-2019, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T07:58:59-08:00","id":1349340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349334#post1349334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to take Accelerator's Killing Cloud as a spell, why would I pick up Death of Obsidian Butterflies after?<br /> <br /> \u200bLike, if you want this to be Terrestrial, what's the downside that stops this from being a technically superior version of DoOB? It's more precise <i>and</i> does more damage <i>and</i> leaves inorganic stuff like money, armor and weapons undamaged for looting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me check something first. <br /> <br /> Death by obsidian butterflies: <br /> <br /> 30 yards wide, 100 yards long, 10 yards high, according to 2e. <br /> <br /> Fine then. Then let's have my spell reach 50 yards. <br /> <br /> Yards = metres, by my rough estimate. That means, what, you cut my range in half? Does that count? Basically, if you want wholesale destruction? You choose Death by obsidian butterlies. You wanna hit something that's closer, and surrounded by more stuff? You choose my killing cloud spell. Maybe you can also make it so that no, it corrodes away everything on a person. What I'm thinking of is combat within a place like 'stone walls' and 'iron pillars'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T04:13:50-08:00","id":1349539,"title":"","content":"So I've been thinking. Is a small delivery spell that can let you transport books, scrolls, small figurines, and letters considered to be too much? I've been thinking of putting in a clause saying 'you can only send this to someone with whom you have a positive intimacy' and 'nothing bigger than a book'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:01:10-08:00","id":1349545,"title":"","content":"Why not just have an elemental or a demon deliver it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:32:59-08:00","id":1349548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349545#post1349545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just have an elemental or a demon deliver it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow. I can do that? Is it actually, you know, acceptable to have design space for super-fast demon delivery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:36:40-08:00","id":1349550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349548#post1349548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow. I can do that? Is it actually, you know, acceptable to have design space for super-fast demon delivery?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, you got an agatae right there. Bind it for a year, then use it as a courier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:54:15-08:00","id":1349555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349548#post1349548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow. I can do that? Is it actually, you know, acceptable to have design space for super-fast demon delivery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agata can fly thirty miles per hour while carrying two armored men on its back, and once it's reached the target of your delivery, it can Hurry Home to your side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-19-2019, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:59:44-08:00","id":1349558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349550#post1349550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, you got an agatae right there. Bind it for a year, then use it as a courier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But I want to have, like....<br /> <br /> <i>You see a bird flying towards you. Then you realize that it's far too box-shaped. And then, your eyes widen as you realize that it's coming straight towards your window. Your mouth opens into a wide-scream, as you anticipate the shattering glass... only for the bird-like thing to pass through harmlessly. The strange creatures circled your room once, twice, and then slowed down. You look at it, mouth wide open, earlier shock gone. The thing looked like some kind of squarish package... with two glowing wings on it? <br /> <br /> Then the wings disappeared with a poof, and the package dropped to the floor with a thud. A small chime came out, saying &quot;Package delivered.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:08:03-08:00","id":1349563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349558#post1349558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. But I want to have, like....<br /> <br /> <i>You see a bird flying towards you. Then you realize that it's far too box-shaped. And then, your eyes widen as you realize that it's coming straight towards your window. Your mouth opens into a wide-scream, as you anticipate the shattering glass... only for the bird-like thing to pass through harmlessly. The strange creatures circled your room once, twice, and then slowed down. You look at it, mouth wide open, earlier shock gone. The thing looked like some kind of squarish package... with two glowing wings on it?<br /> <br /> Then the wings disappeared with a poof, and the package dropped to the floor with a thud. A small chime came out, saying &quot;Package delivered.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you really wanted, I'd just...make that a weird demon yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:18:59-08:00","id":1349568,"title":"","content":"I'd see that as more one of the weird sort of things a Second Circle demon could do for its summoner; sort of like how Florivet might grant favorable winds to someone, there could be a demon citizen out there who can touch an object to make it sprout wings and fly to a given recipient.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I wouldn't make it a first circle though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:25:44-08:00","id":1349572,"title":"","content":"A Terrestrial spell that lets you do drone deliveries sounds fun. Maybe just add a way for the recipient to refuse the package and return it to sender, to avoid the spell being used for bomb delivery, otherwise what you have sounds good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:32:09-08:00","id":1349574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349572#post1349572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Terrestrial spell that lets you do drone deliveries sounds fun. Maybe just add a way for the recipient to refuse the package and return it to sender, to avoid the spell being used for bomb delivery, otherwise what you have sounds good.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said that it should only be for people you have positive intimacies for. <br /> <br /> You wanna bomb that meeting? You better send a grenade to someone you like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T11:18:58-08:00","id":1349632,"title":"","content":"I feel that this proposed spell is a bit more potent than Infallible Messenger, but not quite so potent as to necessitate a Celestial spell - hence why I suggested it instead be a power of a Second Circle Demon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T11:47:05-08:00","id":1349638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349632#post1349632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that this proposed spell is a bit more potent than Infallible Messenger, but not quite so potent as to necessitate a Celestial spell - hence why I suggested it instead be a power of a Second Circle Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give an example of a use of the spell that would be overtuned for the Terrestrial Circle of Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T12:13:29-08:00","id":1349646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349638#post1349638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give an example of a use of the spell that would be overtuned for the Terrestrial Circle of Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give it a shot.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Uncanny Swift Parcel Spirit</b><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Cost:</b> Ritual, 2wp<br /> \u200b<b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> \u200b<b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> \u200bThe sorcerer treats a square of paper with gum from an acacia tree, and applies to it the sigil of any of the gods of travel, investing it with a measure of Essence. This stamped paper may be applied to an ordinary object weighing up to ten pounds, causing a winged spirit to form around the object. The spirit can be directed to fly to any recipient to whom the sorcerer bears a positive Tie, traveling immaterially at 60 miles per hour. Once it comes within Short Range of the recipient, it materializes and announces its presence and sender. The recipient may choose to accept the gift, at which point the spirit dissipates, leaving behind the object; if the recipient refuses the gift, the spirit returns to the sorcerer before dissipating.<br /> <br /> \u200bA sorcerer who takes Uncanny Swift Parcel Spirit as his control spell may use rare inks and other arcane ingredients (a Resources 3 purchase) to make an express stamp, creating a spirit that moves even more swiftly, able to travel at twice the speed of its brethren and able to carry as much as a ton.<br /> <br /> \u200b...eh, I still don't like it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-19-2019, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T12:25:14-08:00","id":1349648,"title":"","content":"I actually like that one a lot, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> - Well done <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Yoinked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:06:03-08:00","id":1349655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349646#post1349646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll give it a shot.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Uncanny Swift Parcel Spirit</b><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Cost:</b> Ritual, 2wp<br /> \u200b<b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> \u200b<b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> \u200bThe sorcerer treats a square of paper with gum from an acacia tree, and applies to it the sigil of any of the gods of travel, investing it with a measure of Essence. This stamped paper may be applied to an ordinary object weighing up to ten pounds, causing a winged spirit to form around the object. The spirit can be directed to fly to any recipient to whom the sorcerer bears a positive Tie, traveling immaterially at 60 miles per hour. Once it comes within Short Range of the recipient, it materializes and announces its presence and sender. The recipient may choose to accept the gift, at which point the spirit dissipates, leaving behind the object; if the recipient refuses the gift, the spirit returns to the sorcerer before dissipating.<br /> <br /> \u200bA sorcerer who takes Uncanny Swift Parcel Spirit as his control spell may use rare inks and other arcane ingredients (a Resources 3 purchase) to make an express stamp, creating a spirit that moves even more swiftly, able to travel at twice the speed of its brethren and able to carry as much as a ton.<br /> <br /> \u200b...eh, I still don't like it, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing I worded my question poorly, I was actually wondering what made you think that the spell is beyond the scope of Terrestrial in your opinion - something like &quot;the spell would let you do x, which is too strong/out of theme for Terrestrial&quot;. I do like the version of the spell you came up with though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:19:33-08:00","id":1349661,"title":"","content":"The spell isn't out of <i>scope</i> of Terrestrial. It's just at odds with how I view the setting. People who inquire after the services of sorcerers should do it because they want a demon to kill their hated enemy, or because they want the passphrase that lets them command an ancient golem, not so they can ensure their package is delivered by the next business day.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's why I made the spell a cheeky reference to its real-world counterpart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:27:43-08:00","id":1349688,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the Sorcerer should not let anyone know he has that spell... it is for his personal use, not so that he can be a postmaster sorcerer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T15:05:25-08:00","id":1349698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349688#post1349688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, the Sorcerer should not let anyone know he has that spell... it is for his personal use, not so that he can be a postmaster sorcerer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But how does he use the spell without letting anyone know he has it? The package explicitly states who sent it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T15:40:05-08:00","id":1349707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349698#post1349698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But how does he use the spell without letting anyone know he has it? The package explicitly states who sent it!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You only send packages to people you trust to keep their mouth shut <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And at first glance (and probably second, third and fourth glances), it just looks like you summoned some form of Elemental or Demon to deliver your whatever... so, to be fair, any sorcerer with Summon Elemental or Summon Demon can do this very thing already anyways, without having to purchase a special spell, so...I guess secrecy is moot anyways... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T15:40:52-08:00","id":1349708,"title":"","content":"Darn. I wish I was the one to write that...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349661#post1349661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell isn't out of <i>scope</i> of Terrestrial. It's just at odds with how I view the setting. People who inquire after the services of sorcerers should do it because they want a demon to kill their hated enemy, or because they want the passphrase that lets them command an ancient golem, not so they can ensure their package is delivered by the next business day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. You can do the sorcerer in a lone tower archetype. But I think people should seek out sorcerers for more reasons than that. Namely, because they're useful. A sorcerer with access to skilled help can produce talismans and enchanted potion easier than most humans. A sorcerer can force a field to bring harvest when the crop is destroyed by locust or disease, and end drought with water from stone. A sorcerer can be of use when asking for help from marauding demons like, say, a rogue blood ape or Luminata. Perhaps he can be asked to act as vizier or consultant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T16:19:57-08:00","id":1349714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349661#post1349661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell isn't out of <i>scope</i> of Terrestrial. It's just at odds with how I view the setting. People who inquire after the services of sorcerers should do it because they want a demon to kill their hated enemy, or because they want the passphrase that lets them command an ancient golem, not so they can ensure their package is delivered by the next business day.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's why I made the spell a cheeky reference to its real-world counterpart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, that makes sense. Personally I feel that, like with Infallible Messenger, the 2wp cost is a sufficient deterrent to keep the spell from being used for unimportant reasons, but it's mostly down to personal opinion at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T04:22:14-08:00","id":1350792,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers casting illusions, turning invisible is a source of pulp fiction. Is it suitable for a terrestrial to, say, cast a spell to make sight and sound rolls inapplicable towards himself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T05:47:52-08:00","id":1350800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1350792#post1350792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerers casting illusions, turning invisible is a source of pulp fiction. Is it suitable for a terrestrial to, say, cast a spell to make sight and sound rolls inapplicable towards himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the spell in <i>Dragon-Blooded</i>, &quot;Sculpted Seafoam Eidolon.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T06:22:17-08:00","id":1350808,"title":"","content":"Fuck. Forum ate my post. Can't be bothered. <br /> <br /> Same as sculpted eidolon to pierce the illusion. Same as eyes and ears, but when dealing with things like supersensitive noses, it gets a minus 2 in difficulty. Works on humans, animals, and machines. Extends for Willpower metres, letting you bring in a group. <br /> <br /> If you got an essence pool, you can do things like disguise your group as something else, extend the range, or jack up the difficulty of seeing you. Maybe one for 'attaching' an illusion to a place momentarily, letting you do things like conceal traps or bombs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T20:35:33-08:00","id":1351213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1349688#post1349688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, the Sorcerer should not let anyone know he has that spell... it is for his personal use, not so that he can be a postmaster sorcerer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he can only send packages to someone for whom he has a positive Tie, so the only way to play post office with this spell is if you've got a postsorcerer in every major city and they're <i>all</i> buddies.<br /> <br /> As far as demons go, Makarios has a Charm called Gates of the Dreaming Market that lets him exchange physical objects with someone he meets in a dream. (This is far from the only reason a sorcerer engaging in interstate commerce might want Makarios on hand.) It's even learnable by Eclipses, and doesn't seem to have any distance limit, so it's actually a <i>very</i> good way to transfer objects around Creation (or even other realms of existence, I guess). So clearly, a Second Circle demon (or equivalently powerful spirit) can be a hell of a courier.<br /> <br /> Also note that any spell or other magic you can use to send stuff to your friends is likely to see heavy use in smuggling and/or spying. Ten pounds isn't much, but many valuable things come in small packages, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T21:16:08-08:00","id":1351218,"title":"","content":"Like, say, notes. Or a valuable sympathetic connection. Or physical evidence. Important documents with signatures you can forge. Or valuable contraband. <br /> <br /> Let's face it. There's probably a smuggling ring somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T11:09:47-08:00","id":1351321,"title":"","content":"REVEALING FROST ATMOSPHERE<br /> Type: ritual<br /> Duration: 3 days<br /> <br /> The sorcerer goes to the cardinal points of the room, casting the rituals of the truth revealed. It is said that each lie coats the heart with a layer of frost, making it colder and harder. The sorcerer brings this to the forefront.<br /> <br /> From that point on, anyone who enters the room and speaks a lie must roll as if they are against judges ear technique. Detection of a lie would cause their breathe to form a mist, as if they were standing in a northern winter.<br /> <br /> ENFORCED OBEDIENCE STARE<br /> Cost: 10m<br /> <br /> The sorcerer's eyes flash mercilessly, like the glowing eyes of a predator shining in the darkness. This functions similarly to Peacock Shadow Eyes. Instead of forcing the target to accept a new belief, the target is forced to answer the sorcerer's questions. After the spell is released, the victim simply feels as if he had just spoken an ordinary conversation with the sorcerer<br /> <br /> THE WIND'S OF FORGETFULNESS<br /> Cost: 10m<br /> Range: medium range<br /> <br /> The sorcerer clips his hands, and a wind of forgetfulness and dementia runs through the area, swarming through every nook and cranny, entering one ear and out of the other, stealing away memories and facts. This can only steal memories that were formed no later than 2 days ago. After the theft, the sorcerer can simply leave their minds blank... Or he can roll occult + intelligence against their perception + awareness. Failure means that they realize that their memories had been tampered with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T11:37:26-08:00","id":1351328,"title":"","content":"DEADLY GRANTER OF DISEASE<br /> Type: ritual<br /> <br /> This comes in 2 forms. The sorcerer rolls his occult + intelligence, letting the obtain successes enhance the disease he is creating. Infection requires either touch or the usage of sympathetic links which burn out after use.<br /> <br /> 1. The target is struck by a disease out of nowhere. Successes may be used to vastly increase the morbidity of the disease. Any mortal disease or malady can be used, from tuberculosis to cancer. <br /> <br /> 2. The target is transformed into a carrier, with a difficulty of 4 for a medicine + intelligence roll backed by magic. The target is immune to the disease itself. But from then on, anybody he touches or anything he handles is infected, spreading death and destruction wherever he goes. The disease spreads with a virulence that can be increased via the previous roll, but once it has infected someone else the increased virulence is reduced back to normal. This lasts for an entire season.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T20:05:01-08:00","id":1351403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1351321#post1351321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ENFORCED OBEDIENCE STARE<br /> Cost: 10m<br /> <br /> The sorcerer's eyes flash mercilessly, like the glowing eyes of a predator shining in the darkness. This functions similarly to Peacock Shadow Eyes. Instead of forcing the target to accept a new belief, the target is forced to answer the sorcerer's questions. After the spell is released, the victim simply feels as if he had just spoken an ordinary conversation with the sorcerer</div> </div> </div> </div>Peacock Shadow Eyes is already just as capable of getting someone to answer questions as it is of getting someone to accept a new belief, isn't it? There's no reason you can't do pretty much any kind of social influence with the entranced victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T06:10:49-08:00","id":1351461,"title":"","content":"Peacock eyes and dream mist I think cover a lot of the illusion side of sorcery but turning invisible without stepping on the toes of stealth is a bit harder. I might allow a spell to make you hazy or translucent. Perhaps a spell letting you slip out of existence for a short while making you unfindable but also preventing you from interacting with the world. You could merge with an object or building and be able to travel inside of it effectively invisible? I wouldn't allow just straight invisibility. Or anything that would step on Sound and Sent banishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T00:20:54-08:00","id":1351607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deamonlight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1351461#post1351461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Peacock eyes and dream mist I think cover a lot of the illusion side of sorcery but turning invisible without stepping on the toes of stealth is a bit harder. I might allow a spell to make you hazy or translucent. Perhaps a spell letting you slip out of existence for a short while making you unfindable but also preventing you from interacting with the world. You could merge with an object or building and be able to travel inside of it effectively invisible? I wouldn't allow just straight invisibility. Or anything that would step on Sound and Sent banishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a spell for turning yourself immaterial. <br /> <br /> I think i should make it so you can toggle the materialisation on and off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T10:34:19-08:00","id":1369403,"title":"","content":"Over in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369368-solar-sorcery\">this thread</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25965-tonkku\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25965\" data-vbnamecard=\"25965\">Tonkku</a> requested a Solar Circle spell to trap people and objects in a painting. I figured I'd repost my attempt here, to keep things in one collected place.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Fidelity of Images</span><br /> Cost: </b>50sm, 3wp OR Ritual, 4wp OR Ritual, 5wp<br /> Keywords:None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> The sorcerer speaks the Mudra of Referent-Symbol Equivalence, the proscribed dictum uttered by one of the lost titans, that states that an object and that which describes it are the same. A blank canvas of shining white appears before her, and she begins to paint, colors streaming from her fingers or simply appearing on the blank sheet as she gazes at it. What she beholds in front of her is faithfully reproduced on the canvas, and when she is done, there is no difference between the two - only the painting remains.<br /> <br /> This spell can be used in three different ways. The first version, usable in combat, targets a single character or an object no larger than 5 yards in its longest dimension. Once the sorcerous motes listed above have been gathered, the sorcerer makes a special gambit. She rolls (Intelligence + Occult) against the target's Resolve to hit, and this attack is considered undodgeable and unblockable (an object on someone's person use the owner's Resolve, while unattended objects have an effective Resolve of 1). If she hits, the difficulty of the gambit is equal to the target's current temporary Willpower, or 3, whichever is higher. If the initiative roll for the gambit succeeds, the target vanishes, and is effectively stored in the painting.<br /> <br /> The second version is cast ritually, over the course of a day, starting at dawn and ending at dusk, costs 4wp, and can effect an area with a diameter of (EssenceX100) yards. During the ritual, various signs and portents appear within the area to be affected that indicate that something strange is going on (rolls of ([Intelligence or Wits] + Occult), difficulty 3, can identify the specific spell), and the sorcerer must paint in a location that allows her to see the majority of the area, and thus must be visible to the majority of the inhabitants as well. She may not perform any other activity, and any significant disruption or distraction (<i>especially</i> being forced to roll Join Battle) will end the ritual without effect. Once the ritual is complete, the sorcerer rolls (Intelligence + Occult) once, and compares her result to the Resolve of all who remain in the area at that time. Anyone whose Resolve she beats are taken into the painting, as are all inanimate objects and the terrain within the area.<br /> <br /> The third version works much like the second, except that it costs 5wp, can effect an area of up to (Essence) miles, and the ritual takes 7 days, during which the sorcerer must wander the area to be affected, sufficient to see a majority of it. She may pause the ritual to sleep and eat, but otherwise must continue it uninterrupted, as per the second version. At the end of the ritual, again like the second version, she must roll (Intelligence + Occult) against the Resolve of everyone who remains in the area, and all who she overcomes, and all the objects and terrain in the area, are taken into the painting.<br /> <br /> In all cases, people, objects, and terrain taken into a painting are effectively held in stasis - no time passes for them, they need no food or water, and will never age or decay. If terrain or large objects are taken up by this spell, what remains is &quot;generic&quot; terrain suitable for the region of Creation it was in: a grassy field in the East, empty sand in the Burning Waste of the South, a sandy islet or open sea in the West, and so on. <br /> <br /> The painting itself is vulnerable to damage, though it is far tougher than a mundane canvas, requiring effort and magic similar to that required to damage artifacts in order to harm it. <br /> <br /> The process of conversion to a painted image can be reversed. The sorcerer casting the spell must have the painting in hand (though it need not be a painting they themselves created). This always requires a casting of the second version of the spell, regardless of how many people or how large an area were originally contained. The people or objects take shape in the area before the sorcerer during the course of the ritual, finally jerking into motion and life again at its completion. If the painting contained terrain, it is &quot;mixed&quot; with the existing terrain, without significantly displacing existing features or overlapping anything. If this can't be done, the spell automatically fails. For example, if a painting of a forest scene were to be overlaid with an existing forest, the result would be a much-denser wood, with approximately twice as many trees packed together. However, the same forest scene could not be overlaid on an existing fortress or city, because the trees could not fit in with the buildings without displacing or overlapping with them.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer who chooses The Fidelity of Images as her control spell can interact with the paintings she creates much more comprehensively. While holding or regarding a painting, she may spend a point of temporary willpower to enter it. Doing so puts her in a pocket dimension of sorts, where the terrain and people in the painting exist. While the sorcerer is in the painting, time passes normally there, and she can interact with anything there just as she could in the real world. <br /> <br /> Outside of the scene contained in the painting, the pocket world is a flat white expanse stretching into infinity, the same color as the blank canvas. A sorcerer in the painting can expand it by casting the spell, using the second version with the day-long ritual. Treat each such casting as one phase of Wyld-Shaping Technique, except that she rolls (Intelligence + Occult) in place of (Intelligence + Lore), there is no encounter roll, and she may never do more than 7 phases of creation (which requires that she cast the spell 7 times in sequence).<br /> <br /> Terrain, objects, and people created in the pocket dimension of the painting can also be expelled into the real world. To do so, the sorcerer must spend 3wp while holding the painting to change its viewpoint to the new area she wants to make real. If some but not all of the pocket dimension is taken into the real world this way, the missing patches will appear in the painting's pocket dimension as blank, empty stretches of canvas.<br /> <br /> <i>Distortion </i>(Goal number 30): Distorting The Fidelity of Images requires that the distorting sorcerer target one of the paintings created by the spell, not the casting sorcerer. Successfully distorting the painting allows the distorting caster to change one major detail of the painting. A person could change appearance, a forest could transform into a different type of tree, a fortress could shift its design, and so on. The changes are limited to what a skilled painter could do to an existing artwork without completely destroying it, and transformations to people are always cosmetic - a woman from the South could be given the blue hair and brown skin of a native of the West, but when released from the painting, her memories, Intimacies, and other features of her mind would remain the same. <br /> A caster may distort their <i>own</i> casting of The Fidelity of Images, if she wants to transform something caught in the painting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T13:21:48-08:00","id":1369433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1369403#post1369403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first version, usable in combat, targets a single character or an object no larger than 5 yards in its longest dimension. Once the sorcerous motes listed above have been gathered, the sorcerer makes a special gambit. She rolls (Intelligence + Occult) against the target's Resolve to hit, and this attack is considered undodgeable and unblockable (an object on someone's person use the owner's Resolve, while unattended objects have an effective Resolve of 1). If she hits, the difficulty of the gambit is equal to the target's current temporary Willpower, or 3, whichever is higher. If the initiative roll for the gambit succeeds, the target vanishes, and is effectively stored in the painting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm worried that this would boil down to instant victory if it went off. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T16:03:40-08:00","id":1369465,"title":"","content":"Yeah...while gathering 50sm in combat is hardly a walk in the park, it seems rather difficult to resist.<br /> <br /> The victim's options would appear to boil down to 1) use Seven Shadow Evasion or 2) be a painting.<br /> <br /> Or is this within the category of stuff that Destiny-Manifesting Method would protect you from? I guess being trapped in a painting probably counts as &quot;reality-shaping.&quot;<br /> <br /> The second and third versions seem a lot more fair, since the roll to recognize the signs and portents isn't that hard (for heroic characters anyway) and stopping the ritual is pretty easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T16:41:43-08:00","id":1369471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1369465#post1369465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...while gathering 50sm in combat is hardly a walk in the park, it seems rather difficult to resist.<br /> <br /> The victim's options would appear to boil down to 1) use Seven Shadow Evasion or 2) be a painting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>is</i> Solar Circle. Compare this to Death Ray, which a) hits all targets out to short range on the <i>first</i> round, b) gets (Essence) bonus successes to hit, and c) gets threshold successes + current temporary willpower bonus dice on the damage roll. And <i>then</i> it doesn't even reset you to base, you can just keep blasting people, with the same attack roll, no less!<br /> <br /> This one, by contrast, a) doesn't add anything to the attack roll or the roll to confirm the gambit besides what you can pour in with Excellency, b) only targets one creature, c) can be defended against with appropriate charms like Seven Shadows Evasion or Heavenly Guardian Defense, and d) <i>does</i> go up against Resolve, meaning anything that boosts Resolve can boost the defense. All things considered, I think they're comparable, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is this within the category of stuff that Destiny-Manifesting Method would protect you from?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd certainly allow it to protect you, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T18:58:38-08:00","id":1369482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1369471#post1369471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it <i>is</i> Solar Circle. Compare this to Death Ray, which a) hits all targets out to short range on the <i>first</i> round, b) gets (Essence) bonus successes to hit, and c) gets threshold successes + current temporary willpower bonus dice on the damage roll. And <i>then</i> it doesn't even reset you to base, you can just keep blasting people, with the same attack roll, no less!<br /> <br /> This one, by contrast, a) doesn't add anything to the attack roll or the roll to confirm the gambit besides what you can pour in with Excellency, b) only targets one creature, c) can be defended against with appropriate charms like Seven Shadows Evasion or Heavenly Guardian Defense, and d) <i>does</i> go up against Resolve, meaning anything that boosts Resolve can boost the defense. All things considered, I think they're comparable, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell, to me, reads &quot;Have 12+ Resolve (more if the sorcerer has Charms to boost INT+OCC rolls), have &gt;50% casters Init in WP, or die&quot;. <br /> The first isn't possible unless you're specced for Resolve. <br /> The second depends entirely on how aggressively you have to spend WP. I remind you of the existence of Poised Lion Attitude, among other WP-drainers. <br /> The third is a failstate. <br /> <br /> Death Ray just requires you get a decent Dodge or Parry, then let the caster Crash themselves trying to hit you. <br /> <br /> Which is a combatant more likely to have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T23:38:13-08:00","id":1369520,"title":"","content":"I really liked that version Kelly made. When I was thinking on it, I didn't think of creating one sorcery with the OR effect in choosing what scale to use it which is nice. Now I'm wondering how realistically can one expect to be able to cast say second version without interruption? Could one use say stealth to try stay unnoticed during painting or just need circle mates to stay undisturbed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25965-tonkku","name":"Tonkku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T09:48:47-08:00","id":1370075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1369482#post1369482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spell, to me, reads &quot;Have 12+ Resolve (more if the sorcerer has Charms to boost INT+OCC rolls), have &gt;50% casters Init in WP, or die&quot;.<br /> The first isn't possible unless you're specced for Resolve.<br /> The second depends entirely on how aggressively you have to spend WP. I remind you of the existence of Poised Lion Attitude, among other WP-drainers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do take your point. I still feel that this is possible to defend against (and at 50 sm, will probably be the only spell a sorcerer casts in a combat), but it still might be too potent. What if, instead of a gambit, it was just a decisive attack (still rolled against the target's Resolve as a defense) and the spell only took effect if it reduced the target to incapacitated? Maybe with a clause that said if you didn't reduce the target to incap in one attack, you didn't have to recast the spell, but instead could try again once you built up some initiative again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tonkku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1369520#post1369520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm wondering how realistically can one expect to be able to cast say second version without interruption? Could one use say stealth to try stay unnoticed during painting or just need circle mates to stay undisturbed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote it the way I did specifically to make it difficult to hide during the process. People who don't want to get painted should have an opportunity to protest, I feel. The solution to that is to have defenders that can cope with objections without you having to stop painting, I feel. Most sorcerers should be able to accomplish that, even if they don't have a Circle, since they should be able to summon some pretty potent defenders at this level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T13:32:56-08:00","id":1370136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1370075#post1370075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do take your point. I still feel that this is possible to defend against (and at 50 sm, will probably be the only spell a sorcerer casts in a combat), but it still might be too potent. What if, instead of a gambit, it was just a decisive attack (still rolled against the target's Resolve as a defense) and the spell only took effect if it reduced the target to incapacitated? Maybe with a clause that said if you didn't reduce the target to incap in one attack, you didn't have to recast the spell, but instead could try again once you built up some initiative again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would work. My big concern was it being instant defeat, and that would take that problem away. <br /> I think if it's &quot;just&quot; a normal Decisive against Resolve (barring un-negators) it could also be made significantly cheaper for combat usage if the retry clause wasn't added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T21:58:21-08:00","id":1370236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1370075#post1370075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do take your point. I still feel that this is possible to defend against (and at 50 sm, will probably be the only spell a sorcerer casts in a combat), but it still might be too potent. What if, instead of a gambit, it was just a decisive attack (still rolled against the target's Resolve as a defense) and the spell only took effect if it reduced the target to incapacitated? Maybe with a clause that said if you didn't reduce the target to incap in one attack, you didn't have to recast the spell, but instead could try again once you built up some initiative again?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could make it work like Heart-Eating Fist: a gambit, but the difficulty is equal to the target's remaining health levels. I think that slots into existing game rules more cleanly.<br /> <br /> Being able to build up successes across multiple gambit attempts would be a bit of an odd mechanic. If you don't need to recast the spell (probably fair, demanding 50sm and 3wp all over again would be too much), what <i>do</i> you need to attempt the roll again?<br /> <br /> ...It's a little hard to visualize the scene of a sorcerer who didn't quite trap his target the first time and needs to build up more Initiative, though. &quot;Damn, my painting wasn't quite perfect! I'd better punch this guy a few times and then get back to painting him...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T14:48:58-08:00","id":1370450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1369482#post1369482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spell, to me, reads &quot;Have 12+ Resolve (more if the sorcerer has Charms to boost INT+OCC rolls), have &gt;50% casters Init in WP, or die&quot;. <br /> The first isn't possible unless you're specced for Resolve. <br /> The second depends entirely on how aggressively you have to spend WP. I remind you of the existence of Poised Lion Attitude, among other WP-drainers. <br /> The third is a failstate. <br /> <br /> Death Ray just requires you get a decent Dodge or Parry, then let the caster Crash themselves trying to hit you. <br /> <br /> Which is a combatant more likely to have?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're bringing in charms, then Death Ray and this spell are fairly interchangeable. Moreover, both are only situationally more useful than an Essence 5 Solar attacking with a sword or just talking the fight into not happening.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if we focus on the &quot;trapped&quot; part of trapped in a painting, then the spell gets GM points because it has additional story hooks - the antagonist could be freed by his allies/you can go on a quest to free your circlemate. And, again, if the entity trapped in the painting wasn't just going to be murdered or diplomanced by the Essence 5 Solar casting it, there will be people trying to retrieve them from the painting or steal the painting to use as the lynchpin of a sorcerous working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 02-25-2020, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T14:11:12-07:00","id":1376737,"title":"","content":"So, I came up with this questionable idea. If you compare it to Ivory Orchid Pavilion, it doesn't provide shelter and serves far fewer people (and isn't nearly as ritzy), but provides a serious meal instead of just fruits and nuts. It's a <i>huge</i> step up from Food from the Aerial Table to be sure, but then I always thought that spell was pretty weak. (Sorcery is usually pretty powerful -- a spell that does nothing but produce food should be able to do better than tasteless crap IMO, even at the Terrestrial level.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you're not supposed to be able to easily keep people fed through sorcery, then maybe I've gone too far here. Feedback is, of course, welcome.<br /> <br /> (I did briefly consult CoTD: North for the types of foods a Northern tribe might actually serve at a feast, but I admit I didn't spend terribly long researching.)<br /> <br /> <b>The Chieftain's Table</b> (Celestial Circle Spell)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> Ritual, 2wp<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Twelve hours or until dismissed<br /> <br /> This spell was devised by a mighty Northern chieftain some years after being Chosen by Luna. He wished to be able to properly reward his warriors for a successful battle, and honor important guests, even when the hunting had been poor.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer spends a minute or so speaking an elaborate ritual greeting in Old Realm, inviting those present to dine at his table. As he gestures, up to (sorcerer's Essence) long tables materialize, each with seating for twelve humans and laden with food.<br /> <br /> The food produced by this spell is of the sort that the original chieftain considered worthy of his honored guests: roasted elk and duck, hearty venison stew, smoked fish, crusty bread, barley porridge, a variety of fruits and root vegetables, and plenty of ale and mead. The food is easily sufficient to feed everyone seated at the tables, even if they are all very hungry people with large appetites.<br /> <br /> After twelve hours have passed, the tables vanish, along with all dishes and utensils. (Alternatively, the sorcerer may dismiss the spell early with a brief ritual statement of dismissal.) Any food remaining on the tables vanishes with them; food removed from the tables remains real.<br /> <br /> It is traditionally considered polite when casting this spell to make a small sacrifice to any local deities associated with food (such as field gods, hunting gods, or river gods), lest they be offended at the sorcerer's presumption -- although few deities of that stature are likely to actually make an issue of it, should they feel insulted by a Celestial Exalt.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer who knows The Chieftain's Table as her control spell (for some reason) may vary the offered menu, creating nearly any food and drink she is basically familiar with -- although they must be mundane things of Creation, not (for example) the roasted meat of some bizarre Wyld prodigy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T14:55:15-07:00","id":1376740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376737#post1376737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I came up with this questionable idea. If you compare it to Ivory Orchid Pavilion, it doesn't provide shelter and serves far fewer people (and isn't nearly as ritzy), but provides a serious meal instead of just fruits and nuts. It's a <i>huge</i> step up from Food from the Aerial Table to be sure, but then I always thought that spell was pretty weak. (Sorcery is usually pretty powerful -- a spell that does nothing but produce food should be able to do better than tasteless crap IMO, even at the Terrestrial level.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that Food From the Aerial Table is actually a decent spell, due to the way it was open-ended and hypothetically capable of feeding as many people as you had motes for, in 10-person increments. That's a spell that could pretty easily end hunger, at least locally. I don't know how 3e would implement that, but I'd expect the open-endedness to stay. Anyway, though, I do feel there's room for other food-creating spells, so this is not inherently a bad idea.<br /> <br /> That said, I do feel that the effect of the spell you've got here is a bit too boring and mundane, especially for Celestial Circle. Sorcery, in my opinion, should always <i>feel</i> at least a little weird, and generally have an at least somewhat-permanent effect on the world. Compare Ivory Orchid Pavilion, which creates a Major Intimacy in the people in it, and leaves a patch of white orchids afterwards. This one just creates food and a building, which vanishes after a few hours. <br /> <br /> Honestly, you could probably just vary the fluff of Ivory Orchid Pavilion, just make the food served be stereotypical &quot;chieftan's hall&quot; fare instead of the fruits and nuts. But if you're really looking for a different spell, what about making the feast an &quot;automatic party&quot;, inspiring an emotion of &quot;revelry&quot; or something like that in its inhabitants, and possibly actually summoning local gods of food, drink, and partying to join in. Alternatively, you could tie it to hospitality traditions - it has food and space for everyone who comes in the door, no matter how many. But everyone who enters is bound by the laws of hospitality - guests can't attack their hosts and vice versa, and even insulting or other verbal attacks are punished. Make all of that enforced by the equivalent of an Eclipse oath, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T21:43:27-07:00","id":1376782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376740#post1376740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that Food From the Aerial Table is actually a decent spell, due to the way it was open-ended and hypothetically capable of feeding as many people as you had motes for, in 10-person increments. That's a spell that could pretty easily end hunger, at least locally. I don't know how 3e would implement that, but I'd expect the open-endedness to stay. Anyway, though, I do feel there's room for other food-creating spells, so this is not inherently a bad idea.<br /> <br /> That said, I do feel that the effect of the spell you've got here is a bit too boring and mundane, especially for Celestial Circle. Sorcery, in my opinion, should always <i>feel</i> at least a little weird, and generally have an at least somewhat-permanent effect on the world. Compare Ivory Orchid Pavilion, which creates a Major Intimacy in the people in it, and leaves a patch of white orchids afterwards. This one just creates food and a building, which vanishes after a few hours.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you could probably just vary the fluff of Ivory Orchid Pavilion, just make the food served be stereotypical &quot;chieftan's hall&quot; fare instead of the fruits and nuts. But if you're really looking for a different spell, what about making the feast an &quot;automatic party&quot;, inspiring an emotion of &quot;revelry&quot; or something like that in its inhabitants, and possibly actually summoning local gods of food, drink, and partying to join in. Alternatively, you could tie it to hospitality traditions - it has food and space for everyone who comes in the door, no matter how many. But everyone who enters is bound by the laws of hospitality - guests can't attack their hosts and vice versa, and even insulting or other verbal attacks are punished. Make all of that enforced by the equivalent of an Eclipse oath, perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point of order: the spell as I've written it doesn't actually create shelter. (Maybe it should?) I was sort of envisioning it being cast within an existing longhouse.<br /> <br /> I tend to agree that it could stand to be weirder. While reskinning Ivory Orchid Pavilion to serve different food probably <i>is</i> valid, I like the idea of making it a party spell that creates an atmosphere of revelry. It's fitting, since it was devised by a leader who wanted to reward his underlings by celebrating their success. I also kinda like the idea of local gods showing up, whether invited or not, and expecting a seat of honor at the table. The idea of enforced hospitality is pretty cool, but I think it would actually make the spell noticeably more powerful than IOP, which it probably shouldn't be. (Having enough food and space for all invited guests is an <i>awesome</i> idea that feels suitably mythic, but TBH I feel like being able to feed an <i>unlimited</i> number of people might actually be Solar Circle territory.)<br /> <br /> ...Frankly, you could come up with any number of variations on this sort of thing just by varying the refreshments and the induced mood. Maybe Sijanese sorcerers have a spell that creates elaborate funeral decorations, light finger food for the guests, and a somber mood. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the advice! I will see about doing a rewrite soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T21:58:23-07:00","id":1376783,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that you should be able to choose any kind of food, any kind of sumptious meal, and make the benefits for the control spell something else. Frankly speaking, being able to choose what food you make as a benefit of a control spell seems... lackluster? Boring? Being able to control what you create should be something you have by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T00:26:55-07:00","id":1376787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376783#post1376783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think that you should be able to choose any kind of food, any kind of sumptious meal, and make the benefits for the control spell something else. Frankly speaking, being able to choose what food you make as a benefit of a control spell seems... lackluster? Boring? Being able to control what you create should be something you have by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree.<br /> <br /> When you cast Death By Obsidian Butterflies, you get Obsidian Butterflies. You don't get your choice of wooden hornets or silver moths or bronze locusts.<br /> <br /> The spell does one, fixed, thing.<br /> <br /> The fluff around it making the kind of food the sorcerer who created the spell was familiar with is exactly how sorcery is supposed to work.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree with Kelly that the spell should be weirder. If we're making this an automatic party which gods show up to (and I don't think it should be able to feed infinite people -- I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11237\" data-vbnamecard=\"11237\">Jefepato</a> that sounds Solar), then I see the control benefit allowing variations to the party and the guest list (as well as the types of food).<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Charms Passion Inflaming Artistry (Craft, p. 188) and Sweeten-The-Tap Method (Socialize, p262) might provide some inspiration as to how the party atmosphere might work mechanically.<br /> <br /> How is this for an additional control benefit: The duration is raised to Indefinite. So long as the sorcerer keeps partying they can keep people fed Indefinitely, the spell only ending twelve hours after the sorcerer leaves the feast (and yes, falling asleep is a party foul) or if the sorcerer dismisses it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-27-2020, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T00:58:55-07:00","id":1376790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376787#post1376787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disagree.<br /> <br /> When you cast Death By Obsidian Butterflies, you get Obsidian Butterflies. You don't get your choice of wooden hornets or silver moths or bronze locusts.<br /> <br /> The spell does one, fixed, thing.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. There's obviously a spectrum here. Yes, Death by obsidian butterflies exists. So does raising the Earth's bones. You also get to control where you stormwind rider moves to. There's definitely room for some alteration. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T03:14:26-07:00","id":1376798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376790#post1376790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also get to control where you stormwind rider moves to.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent anyway. You still only get to cross one range band per turn in combat, after all. And it still always manifests as a conjured whirlwind bearing you along; you don\u2019t get to have it take the appearance of a pillar of fire or a beam of light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T08:21:10-07:00","id":1376807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376798#post1376798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To an extent anyway. You still only get to cross one range band per turn in combat, after all. And it still always manifests as a conjured whirlwind bearing you along; you don\u2019t get to have it take the appearance of a pillar of fire or a beam of light.</div> </div> </div> </div>And....<br /> <br /> Oh wow, we need more biblical miracles. <br /> <br /> A spell for creating outbreaks and plagues<br /> <br /> A spell for transmutation of substances (water into wine)<br /> <br /> A spell for.... making the earth swallow up your opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T08:36:11-07:00","id":1376808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376782#post1376782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order: the spell as I've written it doesn't actually create shelter. (Maybe it should?) I was sort of envisioning it being cast within an existing longhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, I misread. Apologies!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[snip] I like the idea of making it a party spell that creates an atmosphere of revelry. [snip] I also kinda like the idea of local gods showing up, whether invited or not, and expecting a seat of honor at the table. The idea of enforced hospitality is pretty cool, but I think it would actually make the spell noticeably more powerful than IOP, which it probably shouldn't be. (Having enough food and space for all invited guests is an <i>awesome</i> idea that feels suitably mythic, but TBH I feel like being able to feed an <i>unlimited</i> number of people might actually be Solar Circle territory.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right that an absolutely unlimited amount of food would probably be unbalanced at Celestial Circle. But here's a thought - you could make this the &quot;hospitality and festival&quot; spell in general. Have it only be castable on certain significant feast days (perhaps always the full moon, but other days in a month are possible, but not <i>every</i> day). When you cast it, you have to specify a group you're inviting to the feast, who are automatically made aware of the invitation if they're within a few hundred miles. Everyone who falls into that group is welcome, and can magically make their way to the location of the feast. Local gods of parties, food, and hospitality are automatically invited, no matter what. The feast automatically expands to include every invited character who attends. When the feast is done, everyone who attended feels an obligation (which manifests as an irreductible, unchangeable Major Intimacy) to repay the caster in kind at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T09:12:10-07:00","id":1376813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376783#post1376783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think that you should be able to choose any kind of food, any kind of sumptious meal, and make the benefits for the control spell something else. Frankly speaking, being able to choose what food you make as a benefit of a control spell seems... lackluster? Boring? Being able to control what you create should be something you have by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit that I was kinda struggling for an idea there -- I had the basic concept of the spell pretty set in my mind, and then realized I had no idea what the control spell benefit should be. (This happens to me a lot when writing spells.)<br /> <br /> That said, there are a <i>lot</i> of spells that only do one fairly specific thing all the time, and I'm sure even the hardiest group of Northern warriors get sick of eating elk eventually.<br /> <br /> I do think having an infinite-duration party works well enough as a control benefit. I suppose I was trying to make it a little more distinct from IOP, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376808#post1376808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right that an absolutely unlimited amount of food would probably be unbalanced at Celestial Circle. But here's a thought - you could make this the &quot;hospitality and festival&quot; spell in general. Have it only be castable on certain significant feast days (perhaps always the full moon, but other days in a month are possible, but not <i>every</i> day). When you cast it, you have to specify a group you're inviting to the feast, who are automatically made aware of the invitation if they're within a few hundred miles. Everyone who falls into that group is welcome, and can magically make their way to the location of the feast. Local gods of parties, food, and hospitality are automatically invited, no matter what. The feast automatically expands to include every invited character who attends. When the feast is done, everyone who attended feels an obligation (which manifests as an irreductible, unchangeable Major Intimacy) to repay the caster in kind at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting idea. I don't really want the spell to only be usable on certain days, but maybe it has an enhanced effect on special feast days (like the thing you suggest where the invited group becomes aware even from a great distance and can travel swiftly to the feast's location)?<br /> <br /> I need to do my rewrite of the basic spell first, but afterwards I'm actually thinking about doing a writeup of a Solar Circle spell that produces an endless banquet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T19:10:14-07:00","id":1376889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376807#post1376807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And....<br /> <br /> Oh wow, we need more biblical miracles.<br /> <br /> A spell for creating outbreaks and plagues<br /> <br /> A spell for transmutation of substances (water into wine)<br /> <br /> A spell for.... making the earth swallow up your opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good thinking. Biblical miracles are certainly a good inspiration for sorcery. (The Parting of the Seas would be one example we already have.)<br /> <br /> I was going to say that transmuting water into wine honestly seems kind of low-key for Exalted sorcery, but looking at the story again...transforming <i>120-180 gallons</i> of water into the finest wine probably <i>is</i> a feat worthy of Terrestrial Circle sorcery.<br /> <br /> (Turning, like, one waterskin of water into decent wine is probably something a thaumaturge could do.)<br /> <br /> Is there not already a spell for some kind of outbreak or plague? I mean, locusts seem highly appropriate. Although in 3e, some of the Biblical plagues seem more like God-King's Shrike effects (although, the problem there is that the ST and not the player decides what sort of doom occurs). And unless you want to create the same plague repeatedly (yikes, dude), a sorcerous working might often make more sense than developing an actual spell.<br /> <br /> We definitely should have a spell for making the earth swallow someone, too, now that Hungry Earth Strike has been nerfed in 3e and can no longer totally bury its victims. Maybe the burial spell could be treated like a gambit roll, with variable difficulty depending on how deep you're trying to sink the poor bastard? For example, the spell could work pretty much like a grapple gambit if you're just trying to sink someone up to their waist in earth and restrain them from moving or dodging effectively, but if you can nail a gambit with a difficulty equal to their remaining health levels (similar to Heart-Eating Fist), you can drop them six feet straight down and leave them there. Or maybe the difficulty could be...I dunno, something like (victim's Strength + Dexterity + Athletics - wound penalty), minimum 6. (I'm taking some vague inspiration from Soul Mastery, here. Which doesn't seem too unfair, since unlike Soul Mastery this isn't <i>instant</i> death and the victim can still be saved.)<br /> <br /> (Now that I think about it, a while back I was contemplating a white jade daiklave called Gravedigger that could do stuff like this. I hadn't gotten very far with the idea though, and that would be a matter for the Artifact/Evocation thread in any case.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:00:32-07:00","id":1376922,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, I can't think of any other biblical miracle that's not used by the spells.<br /> <br /> River of blood is taken<br /> Parting of the Seas is taken <br /> Manna from heaven is taken<br /> Water from stone is taken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:20:23-07:00","id":1376924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376922#post1376922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, I can't think of any other biblical miracle that's not used by the spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Maybe Jesus cursing a tree to death for not being in season?<br /> <br /> Or YHWH afflicting the people of Babel with languages?<br /> <br /> Or maybe Lot\u2019s daughters, who were able to get their father <i>so drunk</i> that he didn\u2019t realize he was impregnating his own children, but somehow kept him able to maintain an erection?<br /> <br /> In Numbers, a donkey spontaneously developed human speech because it was in the presence of an angel.<br /> <br /> There was that time Joshua used Cleromancy to determine who had looted after a battle, and put him <i>and his children</i> to death.<br /> <br /> Making the Sun and the Moon stand in place for more than twenty-four hours is pretty miraculous.<br /> <br /> Or how about Noah cursing his son\u2019s offspring to always be slaves, for the crime of that son having seen him naked?<br /> <br /> What about having she-bears maul children that make fun of you?<br /> <br /> How about Judas casting an illusion that caused one Disciple to see him throwing the thirty silver pieces on the ground and die hanging himself, and another Disciple to see him use the coins to buy a plot of land and die falling headlong and having his guts explode everywhere?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-28-2020, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:34:40-07:00","id":1376928,"title":"","content":"The language thing is... I think there's a spell. Infectious. Lasts a few days or so. <br /> <br /> No alteration of celestial bodies. <br /> <br /> Summoning the army of the wild. <br /> <br /> The rest sound like sorcerous workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:39:07-07:00","id":1376931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376928#post1376928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest sound like sorcerous workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think Jesus spent <i>at least</i> a week on cursing a tree? He pretty much just shouted at it, and it withered and died (or, in another disciple\u2019s version of the story, it withered until it had died the next day).<br /> <br /> The divination used to discover Achan\u2019s looting didn\u2019t seem like a Working, either. Nor the deaths of the children of Korah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-31-2020, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T03:27:42-07:00","id":1376941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376931#post1376931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think Jesus spent <i>at least</i> a week on cursing a tree?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the main plot points in Dynasty of Dovak is a character who spent months secretly performing a working so it <i>looked like</i> she could perform a Celestial working by simply waving her hand and saying Abracadabra.<br /> <br /> Jesus had the showmanship, and he knew the tree would be out of season. Just sayin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T03:32:23-07:00","id":1376942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376941#post1376941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the main plot points in Dynasty of Dovak is a character who spent months secretly performing a working so it <i>looked like</i> she could perform a Celestial working by simply waving her hand and saying Abracadabra.<br /> <br /> Jesus had the showmanship, and he knew the tree would be out of season. Just sayin'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously Jesus was a celestial exalt with a custom charm that replicated the doombot charm, only that instead of 'you killed my fake clone' its 'I appeared to have resurrected'. The touching of hands part was obviously a medical combo.<br /> <br /> edit: The lazarus that walked out of the tomb was not the lazarus that died!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T05:55:31-07:00","id":1376950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376942#post1376942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously Jesus was a celestial exalt with a custom charm that replicated the doombot charm, only that instead of 'you killed my fake clone' its 'I appeared to have resurrected'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says an Exalt can\u2019t elect to use Stealth Charms to stay hidden when their Dual Magnus Prana duplicate is destroyed, and just wait three days to show up again. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Though his resurrection plan might\u2019ve been harder to put in motion if the Romans had just rolled his corpse into an unmarked mass grave with the other criminals (as was typical for people sentenced to death by crucifixion at the time). <i>It sure is convenient</i> that this one time only, they put his body in a tomb, blocked it with a boulder, and posted soldiers to guard it \u2018round the clock.<br /> <br /> Good thing four anonymous accounts of it were recorded decades after it allegedly happened; despite not being entirely consistent with each other on who visited the tomb, at what time, or how many men/angels were there, or whether the resurrected Jesus was there, or whether the stone and soldiers were in place when they got there, or whether they told anybody after, or where the disciples were supposed to meet Jesus after, or even what year it was.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That reminds me: the Gospel of Matthew has a full-on zombie invasion happening at the same time.<br /> <br /> (But that\u2019s probably necromancy I guess.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-28-2020, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T06:14:46-07:00","id":1376953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376950#post1376950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing says an Exalt can\u2019t elect to use Stealth Charms to stay hidden when their Dual Magnus Prana duplicate is destroyed, and just wait three days to show up again.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Though his resurrection plan might\u2019ve been harder to put in motion if the Romans had just rolled his corpse into an unmarked mass grave with the other criminals (as was typical for people sentenced to death by crucifixion at the time). <i>It sure is convenient</i> that this one time only, they put his body in a tomb, blocked it with a boulder, and posted soldiers to guard it \u2018round the clock.<br /> <br /> Good thing four anonymous accounts of it were recorded decades after it allegedly happened; despite not being entirely consistent with each other on who visited the tomb, at what time, or how many men/angels were there, or whether the resurrected Jesus was there, or whether the stone and soldiers were in place when they got there, or whether they told anybody after, or where the disciples were supposed to meet Jesus after, or even what year it was.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That reminds me: the Gospel of Matthew has a full-on zombie invasion happening at the same time.<br /> <br /> (But that\u2019s probably necromancy I guess.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on. Zombie invasion? I did not hear that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T07:20:56-07:00","id":1376958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376953#post1376953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold on. Zombie invasion? I did not hear that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, apparently countless historians and even the writers of the other Gospels didn\u2019t hear it happening; they must have been too busy playing <i>Animal Crossing</i>.<br /> <br /> (Check for yourself: it\u2019s in Matthew 27:52\u201353)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-31-2020, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T07:34:41-07:00","id":1376960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376958#post1376958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, apparently the historians and even the writers of the other Gospels didn\u2019t hear it; they must have been too busy playing <i>Animal Crossing</i>.<br /> <br /> (Check for yourself: it\u2019s in Matthew 27:52\u201353)</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Mother Mercy....</i><br /> <br /> So anyway, remember that whole 'soddom and gomorrah' thing? Someone on Exalted.xi.co made a spell for that. 'Deployment of Martial Weather'. or so it was called. High level spell. <br /> <br /> Wait, I just checked. Its Pyre of armies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T15:46:47-07:00","id":1377003,"title":"","content":"Could a spell make a Withering attack that grants Initiative? Currently there are spells that make a Decisive attack without spending Initiative, and spells that make a Decisive attack that spends Initiative. Would a mass target Withering attack be outside the scope of Sorcery - in particular because it synergizes too much with other combat tactics, making it behave more like a Charm?<br /> <br /> The flavor could be an attack with wind that knocks people back, or any similar magical attack less directly lethal than obsidian butterflies.<br /> <br /> I guess a spell that lets you make a Withering attack on one turn and then continue using for a Decisive attack the next would surely be OK, if a bit overly complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T16:07:57-07:00","id":1377005,"title":"","content":"I suspect the reason we don't see Withering spells is because then sorcerers wouldn't need any of the offensive combat Abilities - they could do combat with only Occult and Dodge. If you want to be a good fighter, you have to be good at fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T16:56:50-07:00","id":1377016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1377005#post1377005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect the reason we don't see Withering spells is because then sorcerers wouldn't need any of the offensive combat Abilities - they could do combat with only Occult and Dodge. If you want to be a good fighter, you have to be good at fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you need the offensive combat Abilities now? You can use DoOB to attack on low Initiative and incidental Initiative gain from other Charms to regain what's lost by the occasional miss, to avoid being Crashed.<br /> <br /> I agree such a spell would make combat sorcerers more powerful, unless it was designed as so inefficient to be useless. That may be a reason not to make it.<br /> <br /> But I think such a charm would be used as often to gain Initiative and then set up a Decisive attack from an ordinary Ability as the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T17:28:01-07:00","id":1377021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1377016#post1377016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need the offensive combat Abilities now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some attacks cannot be dodged, necessitating you either resort to Parry or Seven Shadow Evasion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1377016#post1377016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use DoOB to attack on low Initiative and incidental Initiative gain from other Charms to regain what's lost by the occasional miss, to avoid being Crashed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about when someone hits you? Withering attacks are <i>by design</i> pretty easy to land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T17:42:51-07:00","id":1377024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1377021#post1377021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some attacks cannot be dodged, necessitating you either resort to Parry or Seven Shadow Evasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this spell wouldn't help much with that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about when someone hits you? Withering attacks are <i>by design</i> pretty easy to land. </div> </div> </div>That's true, I'm used to the powerful Solar Melee defensive package, which lets you tank a LOT of Withering attacks from weaker foes. It's totally possible to recover from Crash and get to a reasonable Initiative just off the Initiative you gain from people missing you. But the situation wouldn't be the same here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T09:41:58-07:00","id":1377358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1376889#post1376889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is good thinking. Biblical miracles are certainly a good inspiration for sorcery. (The Parting of the Seas would be one example we already have.)<br /> <br /> I was going to say that transmuting water into wine honestly seems kind of low-key for Exalted sorcery, but looking at the story again...transforming <i>120-180 gallons</i> of water into the finest wine probably <i>is</i> a feat worthy of Terrestrial Circle sorcery.<br /> <br /> (Turning, like, one waterskin of water into decent wine is probably something a thaumaturge could do.)<br /> <br /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for ignoring the rest of your post. But I just found something. I think. According to touhou, there's a creature that can convert water into alcohol, and when ingested, can make a person incapable of getting drunk. <br /> <br /> How about either a spell or demon that can do this? Turn water into other kinds of liquid. One for turning water into wine. Another for turning water into soup. <br /> <br /> And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T16:15:02-07:00","id":1381126,"title":"","content":"A highly experimental shaping ritual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sorcerer's power eats at her, growing hot and swollen as her body wastes away. This manifests as a chronic, supernatural disease with a Morbidity of 3 and an interval of one week. It can't spread to others, nor can it be permanently cured; the sorcerer keeps making weekly (Stamina + Resistance) rolls while in remission, her condition returning to Minor intensity on a failure. In addition to the normal effects of a disease, the sorcerer's condition can grant her sorcerous motes in the following ways:<ul><li>Whenever she loses a point of Willpower or suffers a botch due to her condition; <i>5 sorcerous motes</i>.</li> <li>If she goes a session without losing Willpower or suffering a botch; <i>(Intensity) sorcerous motes</i>.</li> <li>When the intensity of her condition is reduced by a successful (Stamina + Resistance) roll; <i>(original Intensity) sorcerous motes</i>.</li> </ul><br /> All sorcerous motes gained last until the end of the current story, and can be spent towards any spell the sorcerer casts. </div> </div> </div> It definitely needs some fine-tuning, <i>particularly</i> a cap on how many sorcerous motes you can carry at one time. Ideally, it should be tight enough that you can't just amass an effectively bottomless pool, but not so restrictive as to render the punishing Defining symptom (one automatic botch or -1 Willpower, plus 5 sorcerous motes, <i>per scene</i>) useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T06:20:35-07:00","id":1381625,"title":"","content":"<b>Glyphs of Sweet Passing</b> (Labyrinth Circle Ritual)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> Ritual, 3wp<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Target</b>: (Essence x 20 yards)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> (Essence hours)<br /> <br /> This ritual expands upon the spell Rune of Sweet Passing. However, instead of targeting a living creature, the ground itself may be targeted. So that all who die on said grounds automatically become ghosts rather than passing to Lethe. Like Rune of Sweet Passing, souls who die on this tained ground cannot be sent to Lethe by a Zenith's anima power.<br /> <br /> This requires a massive amount of honey (resource 3 amount of honey), blood and graveyard earth for the necromancer and any thaumaturgic assistants to paint and work into the ground. This can be painted into the walls of buildings as well. <br /> <br /> When a person dies on these tainted lands, supernatural bees release from the ground to race to the necromancer and inform them of a subjects death. The necromancer is informed of the sex, rough age, and what type of being they are. (Mortal, Fae, Solar, Lunar, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T09:52:54-07:00","id":1381671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1381625#post1381625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Glyphs of Sweet Passing</b> (Labyrinth Circle Ritual)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this works. However, as I've been converting necromancy spells to 3e myself, I'd suggest that using a spell for Rune of Sweet Passing/Gentle Call of Lethe is the wrong approach. They're a bit too specific and only conditionally useful. Instead, I said that they were both common necromantic workings (Iron Circle Ambition 2). I think the logic there holds for this effect too, and I'd put it at Onyx Circle Ambition 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:42:30-07:00","id":1381698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1381671#post1381671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this works. However, as I've been converting necromancy spells to 3e myself, I'd suggest that using a spell for Rune of Sweet Passing/Gentle Call of Lethe is the wrong approach. They're a bit too specific and only conditionally useful. Instead, I said that they were both common necromantic workings (Iron Circle Ambition 2). I think the logic there holds for this effect too, and I'd put it at Onyx Circle Ambition 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that works. <br /> <br /> I figure it would have be a working. I just thought that is what the ritual meant as I am not too familiar yet with E3 sorcery and workings.<br /> <br /> Mostly in the game I GM in the north I figure that the local deathlord would design this working to invert a part of Traveler's Road in the Shadowland. Or attempt to. The players might find it suspicious that suddenly a lot of honey and honeybees are being purchased and sent into the shadowland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T11:15:14-07:00","id":1381710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1381698#post1381698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure it would have be a working. I just thought that is what the ritual meant as I am not too familiar yet with E3 sorcery and workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between spells and workings in 3e is that each spell is learned separately, paying XP for it, and then the character can cast it as many times as they like (although they have to pay whatever ritual costs it includes every time). A working, on the other hand, is something any sorcerer/necromancer could attempt, using their generic &quot;power of sorcery&quot; to enact the change. Each individual working costs some XP, but that's usually cheaper individually than a spell (an Ambition 2 working costs 4 XP, and a spell if Occult is a favored Ability is 8 XP). Workings usually take longer than most spells, though (they're an extended roll with an interval of one week, so at least that if not more).<br /> <br /> 3e uses &quot;ritual&quot; in the spell costs for some spells because it was decided that for those spells that required a long ritual and thus couldn't be cast in combat, it was kinda pointless to also specify how many sorcerous motes it took to cast them - most Exalt-level sorcerers would be able to gather the motes long before the ritual completed, and even if they didn't, unless you make the Shape Sorcery actions take much longer on such spells, they'd just finish gathering the motes very shortly after the ritual was done. So it was simpler to just say that such spells had a cost of &quot;do the ritual&quot; and assume that it took however long that ritual did to gather them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T03:36:25-07:00","id":1382703,"title":"","content":"I was hoping in creating new custom sorcery shaping ritual using integrity. I'm still short on details but idea was to have some kind of self perfection meditation themed. One where they could for example meditate for internal pool of sorcerous motes they could used during day. I'm open for any feedback and ideas to have actual content and details instead of just vague idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25965-tonkku","name":"Tonkku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T06:15:56-07:00","id":1382730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tonkku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1382703#post1382703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping in creating new custom sorcery shaping ritual using integrity. I'm still short on details but idea was to have some kind of self perfection meditation themed. One where they could for example meditate for internal pool of sorcerous motes they could used during day. I'm open for any feedback and ideas to have actual content and details instead of just vague idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>This exact thing is in Heirs to the Shogunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T06:53:08-07:00","id":1382742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tonkku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1382703#post1382703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping in creating new custom sorcery shaping ritual using integrity. I'm still short on details but idea was to have some kind of self perfection meditation themed. One where they could for example meditate for internal pool of sorcerous motes they could used during day. I'm open for any feedback and ideas to have actual content and details instead of just vague idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are several extant shaping rituals you could use as a basis. Just sticking to the ones in the corebook:<br /> <br /> The second ritual of the Soul-Perfecting Elixir (p. 469) is pretty much exactly what you want. All you'd need to do is replace Stamina with Integrity in the calculations. This initiation also has some highly relevant Merits.<br /> <br /> The third ritual of the Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes (p. 470) allows you to commit motes during meditation and spend them as sorcerous motes until the end of the day.<br /> <br /> The sample Heptagram ritual (p. 471) can easily be refluffed as meditation. Just make it a (Intelligence + Integrity) roll, or whatever Attribute you feel fits for meditation. If you want to make it a bit more flexible, remove the potential dice bonuses to instead make the roll daily instead of once-per-story (though this should replace your previous stock of sorcerous motes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T11:31:05-07:00","id":1382801,"title":"","content":"I posted the first draft of this spell a few pages back. With input from the thread, I've made some updates.<br /> <br /> I ended up slightly increasing the spell's capacity and having it create an actual building as well, in addition to some of the other changes (I'm particularly fond of the &quot;random divine visitors&quot; aspect). I'm not sure if that makes it too good. Please let me know your thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>The Chieftain's Feast</b> (Celestial Circle Spell)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> Ritual, 2wp<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Twelve hours or until dismissed<br /> <br /> This spell was devised by a mighty Northern chieftain some years after being Chosen by Luna. He wished to be able to properly reward his warriors for a successful battle, and honor important guests, even when the hunting had been poor.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer spends several minutes tracing out the intended position of his spell, before speaking an elaborate ritual greeting in Old Realm. As he speaks, a structure assembles itself before him. The sorcerer may customize the intended floor plan to some extent, but it is always a single-story building of wood and daub, in the fashion of many Northern tribes. (A longhouse is, of course, traditional.) Inside are tables laden with food, and seating sufficient for (sorcerer's Essence * 20) guests.<br /> <br /> The food produced by this spell is of the sort that the original chieftain considered worthy of his honored guests: roasted elk and duck, hearty venison stew, smoked fish, crusty bread, barley porridge, a variety of fruits and root vegetables, and plenty of ale and mead. The food is easily sufficient to feed everyone seated at the tables, even if they are all very hungry people with large appetites -- and even if they stay for the spell's entire duration.<br /> <br /> Anyone entering the building and partaking of the feast is treated as having a Minor Tie of good cheer and jovial enjoyment of the festivities. The emotional effect of the gathering has an interesting side effect: local spirits (generally from no further away than (sorcerer's Essence) miles) often sense that a party is being held by an important personage, and it is not unknown for a god or two to turn up at the party hoping for an invitation, either because they enjoy parties or because they just can't miss an important person's social event. Few gods are powerful or arrogant enough to make outright <i>demands</i> of a powerful sorcerer, but sufficiently important (in their own minds) gods may well pointedly <i>expect</i> to be invited to the party (and given a place of honor at the sorcerer's own table, naturally), and be offended if the sorcerer does not oblige.<br /> <br /> (If the Storyteller is having trouble deciding whether any unexpected guests should turn up, one suggestion is to roll two dice; a number of gods show up at the door equal to the successes rolled. If the Storyteller rolls double 10s, a surprisingly important god appears, often with a small retinue in tow.)<br /> <br /> Fortunately, anyone joining the gathering temporarily gains a Major Principle of &quot;I must conduct myself as a proper guest&quot; until they leave. Anyone accepting (or demanding) an invitation to the feast instinctively understands that they are agreeing to behave themselves according to the rules of hospitality; most attendees do not actually notice this effect, since members of most cultures in Creation consider hospitality important. (Indeed, some sorcerers don't even realize this is part of the spell.) To be sure, very few gods would disgrace themselves by ruining a party. The spell does not compel guests to actually <i>like</i> each other or their host (although it's a good atmosphere in which to make friends), but they can be expected to take any violence outside.<br /> <br /> After twelve hours have passed, the building and tables vanish, along with all dishes and utensils. (Alternatively, the sorcerer may dismiss the spell early with a brief ritual statement of dismissal.) Any food remaining on the tables vanishes with them; food removed from the tables remains real.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer who knows The Chieftain's Table as her control spell may cast it with a duration of Indefinite. The structure and tables remain for as long as the sorcerer remains in the immediate vicinity. The tables always somehow end up with enough food to feed everyone seated therein. (The spell's capacity is not actually infinite, though -- if a thousand people gather outside while the food is brought out to them, there will not be enough.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","user":"Jefepato","date":". 04-20-2020, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T08:35:45-07:00","id":1386979,"title":"","content":"So, a while back we had some discussion about spells inspired by Biblical miracles.<br /> <br /> Beckoning That Which Stirs the Sky (a Terrestrial spell) can change the weather for a few miles around, for a few hours. Rain of Doom (a Solar spell) can drop horrifying acid rain over a small city (or a major district of Nexus) overnight. <br /> <br /> Suppose a sorcerer wanted to summon a terrible downpour of rain that lasted for forty days and forty nights. How large an area could a Solar Circle spell flood in this way?<br /> <br /> (Something like this would be a lot less hellishly deadly than Rain of Doom, since people who didn't live in a valley or something could probably evacuate, but it would still wreak havoc, destroy crops, and do a wide variety of damage.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:30:58-07:00","id":1386988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1386979#post1386979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose a sorcerer wanted to summon a terrible downpour of rain that lasted for forty days and forty nights. How large an area could a Solar Circle spell flood in this way?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the usual rule of thumb I use is that Terrestrial Circle spells can affect an army, Celestial Circle spells can affect a city, and Solar Circle spells can affect a country. Obviously, there are exceptions to this - Rain of Doom, as you note, only gets a city, but it's Solar Circle. So some adjustments have to be made for &quot;intensity&quot; of effect within the area. I think the essential question to ask here, is how much of the Biblical miracle do you want to emulate? Is it just the 40 days and nights of continuous rain? (As an aside, I've been told that the &quot;40 days&quot; used in the original Hebrew text was essentially a synonym for &quot;a very long time&quot;, sort of the way we might say &quot;it rained for <i>ages</i>&quot;, so the intent in the Bible might not have been as precise as it seems.) Or do you want the effect to be &quot;a given region is totally flooded&quot;?<br /> <br /> If it's the first, I think a kingdom-sized region is not unreasonable for the rain to cover - something like (Essence X 50) miles radius? If you cast that in any low-lying area, it's <i>going </i>to flood, even if it might not cover every single bit of land. Also, pretty much everywhere downstream of it will flood too. I think you'd probably have noticeable effects <i>thousands</i> of miles from where you cast the spell. Like, if you cast this over that big lake at the eastern tip of the Grey River, then a week or month later you'd get Great Forks, Nexus, and probably Lookshy all flooding.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to just completely drown a region, and the rain is just a magical means of that happening, effectively depositing more water than would actually be possible, I'd make that a smaller area. However, you could expand the area back out if you were willing to say that, at the end of the flood, the excess water just sort of vanished, rather than spreading out and flooding other regions. So, a Solar Circle spell that drowned a region under, say, 500 feet of water should probably only cover about (Essence X 5) miles radius, and then the water drops by 100 feet every 10 miles outside that, until it's completely down. That creates a &quot;mountain&quot; of water that gently lowers and vanishes when the spell ends. If it didn't vanish, you'd have to make the area <i>much</i> smaller, and probably shallower, because that's a <i>stupendous</i> quantity of water - if it doesn't vanish when the spell ends, but instead pours out and flows over the landscape, that's absolutely devastating, and in a way that's probably very hard for STs to adjudicate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:04:42-07:00","id":1387034,"title":"","content":"What about a golden calf or a statue that just plain erodes away intimacies? Or is that a sorcerous working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T21:21:49-07:00","id":1387643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1386988#post1386988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the usual rule of thumb I use is that Terrestrial Circle spells can affect an army, Celestial Circle spells can affect a city, and Solar Circle spells can affect a country. Obviously, there are exceptions to this - Rain of Doom, as you note, only gets a city, but it's Solar Circle. So some adjustments have to be made for &quot;intensity&quot; of effect within the area. I think the essential question to ask here, is how much of the Biblical miracle do you want to emulate? Is it just the 40 days and nights of continuous rain? (As an aside, I've been told that the &quot;40 days&quot; used in the original Hebrew text was essentially a synonym for &quot;a very long time&quot;, sort of the way we might say &quot;it rained for <i>ages</i>&quot;, so the intent in the Bible might not have been as precise as it seems.) Or do you want the effect to be &quot;a given region is totally flooded&quot;?<br /> <br /> If it's the first, I think a kingdom-sized region is not unreasonable for the rain to cover - something like (Essence X 50) miles radius? If you cast that in any low-lying area, it's <i>going </i>to flood, even if it might not cover every single bit of land. Also, pretty much everywhere downstream of it will flood too. I think you'd probably have noticeable effects <i>thousands</i> of miles from where you cast the spell. Like, if you cast this over that big lake at the eastern tip of the Grey River, then a week or month later you'd get Great Forks, Nexus, and probably Lookshy all flooding.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to just completely drown a region, and the rain is just a magical means of that happening, effectively depositing more water than would actually be possible, I'd make that a smaller area. However, you could expand the area back out if you were willing to say that, at the end of the flood, the excess water just sort of vanished, rather than spreading out and flooding other regions. So, a Solar Circle spell that drowned a region under, say, 500 feet of water should probably only cover about (Essence X 5) miles radius, and then the water drops by 100 feet every 10 miles outside that, until it's completely down. That creates a &quot;mountain&quot; of water that gently lowers and vanishes when the spell ends. If it didn't vanish, you'd have to make the area <i>much</i> smaller, and probably shallower, because that's a <i>stupendous</i> quantity of water - if it doesn't vanish when the spell ends, but instead pours out and flows over the landscape, that's absolutely devastating, and in a way that's probably very hard for STs to adjudicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Continuous rain for an extended period of time was the intent -- the kind of disaster that doesn't kill many people directly (unless they're not able-bodied enough to flee to higher ground), but damages buildings, ruins crops, and makes the area essentially unlivable until it's over. The region doesn't need to be <i>totally</i> flooded, and I would expect only the low-lying areas would end up completely underwater.<br /> <br /> I hadn't even considered how far the effects could potentially spread. That could get seriously ugly.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help. The &quot;just flood this whole region&quot; idea is pretty interesting as well, and could make a hell of a weapon. (And if you follow it up with Atrocious Fire Transformation...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1387034#post1387034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a golden calf or a statue that just plain erodes away intimacies? Or is that a sorcerous working?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it could be an artifact, but if it's largely an effect tied to a fixed location (i.e. that golden calf statue isn't going anywhere) then a sorcerous working probably makes the most sense. If you want it to be a temporary effect -- i.e., a spell that simply manifests in the form of a golden calf when cast, and lasts maybe a scene or a week or something -- that could certainly be a spell, though.<br /> <br /> Did you have any particular mechanics in mind? Is it intended to erode <i>all</i> Intimacies, like you're setting people up for Cup Boils Over or something? Or is it meant to erode some specific Intimacies?<br /> <br /> It should be noted that in 3e, there's a tendency to avoid spells that totally invalidate the need for certain skills. (Consider Peacock Shadow Eyes, which makes your social influence easier to apply but still requires the use of actual social skills.) So something like this would <i>probably</i> manifest in a way that uses the sorcerer's actual Performance or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}